{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_LusiLSkfh8ayGkzRm32GhCKp","content":"1\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\n2\t  \"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\n3\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\n4\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\n5\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\n6\t   task, one run.\n7\t\n8\t   The seam is explicit published-export composition (8.10.11), owned by\n9\t   `yang.call.conformance`: the donor source is published as a module and\n10\t   run unmodified, its named export is read from the donor runtime's global\n11\t   namespace (`globalThis.ts_fn`, PHP's `phpfn` function) and projected into the caller\n12\t   runtime's namespace under the same name, and the caller source runs\n13\t   unmodified. No call node is rewritten and no foreign `:code` extracted:\n14\t   the caller holds the donor's own function cell, as the identity check\n15\t   (`stored === phpfn`) shows.\n16\t\n17\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\n18\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\n19\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. Each case runs\n20\t   linked on the three vector VMs, which must agree.\"\n21\t  (:require\n22\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n23\t    [yang.call.conformance :as xl]))\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\n27\t  (testing \"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\"\n28\t    (is (= \"4\"\n29\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n30\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n31\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\"]))))\n32\t  (testing \"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\"\n33\t    (is (= \"yes\"\n34\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n35\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n36\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\"])))))\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\n40\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n41\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"true 5\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n42\t           (xl/call [:php \"<?php function phpfn($a, $b) { return $a + $b; }\"]\n43\t                    [\"phpfn\"]\n44\t                    [:typescript\n45\t                     \"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\"])))))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(deftest limits-test\n49\t  (testing \"a PHP array returned to TS is an opaque handle, usable in PHP\"\n50\t    (let [src \"<?php function phpfn($a = 7) { return $a === 7 ? [1, 2, 3] : count($a); }\"]\n51\t      ;; the PHP int `count` returns reaches TS as an integer (`3n`), not a\n52\t      ;; JS number: the two preludes keep their own number kinds\n53\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"3n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n54\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n55\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n56\t                      [:typescript \"const h = phpfn(); console.log(phpfn(h));\"])))))\n57\t  (testing \"PHP null is neither JS null nor undefined\"\n58\t    (let [src \"<?php function phpfn() { return null; }\"]\n59\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"false false\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n60\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n61\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n62\t                      [:typescript\n63\t                       \"const n = phpfn(); console.log(n === null, n === undefined);\"]))))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_V0ZCPOWap41NOqyD197yhSlT","content":"1\t(ns yang.call.conformance\n2\t  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n3\t   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n4\t   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n5\t\n6\t   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n7\t   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n8\t   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n9\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`), reads each\n10\t   named export from the donor runtime's global namespace, and projects it\n11\t   into the caller runtime's namespace under the same name; then the caller\n12\t   source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own entry. The composition is\n13\t   a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is rewritten, no foreign\n14\t   `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is inserted, and the\n15\t   projected value is the donor's own function cell (identity survives).\n16\t\n17\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n18\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n19\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n20\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n21\t\n22\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n23\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n24\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php` is published beside them.\n25\t   The AST walker is not a backend: its links are refused until L-b.\"\n26\t  (:require\n27\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n28\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n29\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\n30\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n31\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n32\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n33\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n34\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n35\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n36\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n37\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n38\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n39\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(def ^:private published-php\n43\t  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n44\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n45\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n46\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n47\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n48\t\n49\t\n50\t(defn- parse-ok\n51\t  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n52\t  [parse source]\n53\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\n54\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n55\t      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n56\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n57\t    pk))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(def frontends\n61\t  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n62\t\n63\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n64\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n65\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n66\t   - `:unit`: packet to the unmodified lowered unit, the function its\n67\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\n68\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n69\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table);\n70\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n71\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name (a JS global, a PHP\n72\t     function);\n73\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n74\t  {:typescript\n75\t   {:runtime 'js,\n76\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\n77\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\n78\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\n79\t    :unit #(names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit %)),\n80\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\n81\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\n82\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\n83\t    :render render/output},\n84\t   :php\n85\t   {:runtime 'php,\n86\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\n87\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\n88\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\n89\t    :unit #(u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body %)),\n90\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\n91\t    :read-export (fn [export]\n92\t                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\n93\t    :project (fn [name value]\n94\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n95\t    :render php-h/render}})\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t(defn- profile\n99\t  [frontend]\n100\t  (or (get frontends frontend)\n101\t      (throw (ex-info \"frontend not admitted\" {:frontend frontend}))))\n102\t\n103\t\n104\t(defn publish-donor!\n105\t  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n106\t   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n107\t   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n108\t  ([frontend source]\n109\t   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n110\t  ([frontend source module]\n111\t   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit]} (profile frontend)\n112\t         [refusal-key reason] refusal\n113\t         spec (core-module/module-spec\n114\t                refusal-key reason (h/registry)\n115\t                {:name module,\n116\t                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\n117\t                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n118\t                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source)))]),\n119\t                 :exports '#{body},\n120\t                 :runtime-name runtime,\n121\t                 :runtime-address (address)})\n122\t         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n123\t     {:frontend frontend,\n124\t      :module module,\n125\t      :address (:address result),\n126\t      :links (:links result)})))\n127\t\n128\t\n129\t(defn- runtime-entry\n130\t  \"Require and initialize each distinct runtime of `frontend-keys`, once.\"\n131\t  [frontend-keys]\n132\t  (into [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)]\n133\t        (mapcat (fn [runtime]\n134\t                  [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n135\t                   (u/sexp->uast (list (symbol (str runtime) \"init!\")))]))\n136\t        (distinct (map (comp :runtime profile) frontend-keys))))\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t(defn- donor-run\n140\t  \"The donor module required and its body run under its runtime's entry.\"\n141\t  [{:keys [frontend module]}]\n142\t  [(core-module/require-node module)\n143\t   (u/app (u/v (:run-main (profile frontend)))\n144\t          (u/v (symbol (str module) \"body\")))])\n145\t\n146\t\n147\t(defn export-program\n148\t  \"The program whose value is the donor's `export`, read from its runtime's\n149\t   global namespace after its body ran.\"\n150\t  [donor export]\n151\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))]\n152\t    (u/mark-tails\n153\t      (u/seq-nodes (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor)])\n154\t                           (donor-run donor)\n155\t                           [(u/sexp->uast (read-export export))])))))\n156\t\n157\t\n158\t(defn compose\n159\t  \"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\n160\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\n161\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\n162\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\"\n163\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n164\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\n165\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\n166\t    (u/mark-tails\n167\t      (u/seq-nodes\n168\t        (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor) caller-frontend])\n169\t                (donor-run donor)\n170\t                (map (fn [export]\n171\t                       (let [value (symbol (str \"xlang.export.\" export))]\n172\t                         (u/let1 value\n173\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (read-export export))\n174\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (project export value)))))\n175\t                     exports)\n176\t                [(u/app (u/v run-main) (unit (parse caller-source)))])))))\n177\t\n178\t\n179\t(defn link-source\n180\t  \"The serving composition naming the runtimes and the donor module.\"\n181\t  [{:keys [module address]}]\n182\t  (h/source {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published),\n183\t             'js (:address @h/published),\n184\t             'php (:address @published-php),\n185\t             module address}))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(defn- modules\n189\t  \"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it.\"\n190\t  []\n191\t  (php-prelude/admit (h/registry)))\n192\t\n193\t\n194\t(defn run-program\n195\t  \"`{backend value}` of `ast`, linked against `donor`, on each vector VM.\"\n196\t  [donor ast]\n197\t  (let [src (link-source donor)]\n198\t    (into (sorted-map)\n199\t          (map (fn [backend]\n200\t                 [backend\n201\t                  (vm/value (h/run-linked backend ast {:modules (modules),\n202\t                                                       :link-source src}))]))\n203\t          (keys h/backends))))\n204\t\n205\t\n206\t(defn agreed\n207\t  \"The one value every backend of `results` answered, else\n208\t   `{:disagreement results}`.\"\n209\t  [results]\n210\t  (let [vs (set (vals results))]\n211\t    (if (= 1 (count vs)) (first vs) {:disagreement results})))\n212\t\n213\t\n214\t(defn call\n215\t  \"Publish the donor `[frontend source]`, compose its `exports` into the\n216\t   caller `[frontend source]`, run it on each vector VM and answer the\n217\t   caller's rendered value when every backend agrees (else\n218\t   `{:disagreement {backend rendered}}`).\"\n219\t  [[donor-frontend donor-source] exports [caller-frontend caller-source]]\n220\t  (let [donor (publish-donor! donor-frontend donor-source)\n221\t        render (:render (profile caller-frontend))]\n222\t    (agreed (update-vals (run-program donor (compose donor exports caller-frontend\n223\t                                                     caller-source))\n224\t                         render))))"}
