{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_evxxsV0AoQLJayjIBNMNhnDg","content":"1\t(ns yang.clojure\n2\t  \"Yang Clojure compiler - Compiles Clojure code into Yin VM Universal AST.\n3\t\n4\t  This is the Clojure-specific compiler in the Yang compiler collection.\n5\t  It transforms Clojure s-expressions into the Universal AST format that\n6\t  the Yin VM can execute. It handles:\n7\t  - Literals (numbers, strings, booleans, nil, collections)\n8\t  - Variables (symbols)\n9\t  - Lambda expressions (fn)\n10\t  - Function application (including stream operations via module system)\n11\t  - Conditionals (if)\n12\t  - Let bindings (let)\n13\t  - Top-level definitions via explicit yin/def store effects\n14\t  - Macro definitions (defmacro)\n15\t\n16\t  Macro support (docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md §10.2):\n17\t  - defmacro is a special form that lowers to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...))\n18\t    syntax. The lambda node carries `:macro? true`, a frontend-internal fact\n19\t    the encoder (`yin.vm.encoder/program-batch`) turns into a declaration row;\n20\t    the canonical lambda row has no macro slot.\n21\t  - A macro call is an ordinary application. The frontend does no macro\n22\t    lookup: the row-native expander recognizes the call.\n23\t  - compile-program threads a compile-time macro-env naming the defmacros\n24\t    seen so far, only so the native defn lowering yields to a user defn macro.\n25\t\n26\t  Stream operations (stream/make, stream/put, stream/take, >!, <!) are compiled\n27\t  as regular function applications and resolved through the module system at runtime.\n28\t\n29\t  The compiler is written in .cljc format to run on both JVM and Node.js.\"\n30\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile])\n31\t  (:require [yang.core.call :as call]\n32\t            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t;; Forward declaration for mutual recursion\n36\t(declare compile-form compile-lambda)\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(defn literal?\n40\t  \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n41\t  [form]\n42\t  (or (number? form)\n43\t      (string? form)\n44\t      (true? form)\n45\t      (false? form)\n46\t      (nil? form)\n47\t      (keyword? form)\n48\t      (vector? form)\n49\t      (set? form)\n50\t      (map? form)))\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(defn constant-form?\n54\t  \"True when compiling `form` yields a fixed value independent of the\n55\t   environment: scalars, quoted forms, and collections built entirely from\n56\t   constants. A symbol is never constant (it is a variable reference). A\n57\t   `quote` counts as constant only at the top level: nested inside a\n58\t   collection it must reach compile-form so the quote is stripped and the\n59\t   inner form evaluated as data.\"\n60\t  ([form] (constant-form? form true))\n61\t  ([form top-level?]\n62\t   (cond\n63\t     (or (nil? form) (number? form) (string? form)\n64\t         (true? form) (false? form) (keyword? form)) true\n65\t     (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) true\n66\t     (seq? form) (and top-level? (= 2 (count form)) (= 'quote (first form)))\n67\t     (or (vector? form) (set? form)) (every? #(constant-form? % false) form)\n68\t     (map? form) (and (every? #(constant-form? % false) (keys form))\n69\t                      (every? #(constant-form? % false) (vals form)))\n70\t     :else false)))\n71\t\n72\t\n73\t(defn- compile-constructed-collection\n74\t  \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n75\t   existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n76\t   elements like Clojure. Constant collections stay :literal nodes.\n77\t\n78\t   [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n79\t   #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n80\t   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\"\n81\t  [form tail? env macro-env]\n82\t  (let [ctor (cond\n83\t               (vector? form) ['conj []]\n84\t               (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n85\t               :else ['assoc {}])\n86\t        [op seed] ctor\n87\t        args (if (map? form)\n88\t               (into [] (interleave (keys form) (vals form)))\n89\t               (vec form))\n90\t        call {:type :application,\n91\t              :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\n92\t              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}]\n93\t                              (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) args))}]\n94\t    (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t(def initial-macro-env\n98\t  \"Compile-time map of macro names known before any defmacro: none. The\n99\t   standard forms live in the expander's store, not here.\"\n100\t  {})\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t(defn- shadow-macro-env\n104\t  \"Remove shadowed names from the macro environment.\"\n105\t  [macro-env names]\n106\t  (apply dissoc macro-env names))\n107\t\n108\t\n109\t(defn- strip-symbol-meta\n110\t  \"Return an equal symbol without reader metadata.\"\n111\t  [sym]\n112\t  (if (namespace sym)\n113\t    (symbol (namespace sym) (name sym))\n114\t    (symbol (name sym))))\n115\t\n116\t\n117\t(defn- body-expression\n118\t  [body-forms]\n119\t  (cond\n120\t    (empty? body-forms) nil\n121\t    (= 1 (count body-forms)) (first body-forms)\n122\t    :else (cons 'do body-forms)))\n123\t\n124\t\n125\t(defn- mentions-recur?\n126\t  \"True when `form` holds a recur that could target the enclosing function:\n127\t   quoted data and nested fn/loop/def forms own their own recurs.\"\n128\t  [form]\n129\t  (cond\n130\t    (seq? form) (let [head (first form)]\n131\t                  (cond\n132\t                    (= 'recur head) true\n133\t                    (contains? #{'quote 'fn 'loop 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} head) false\n134\t                    :else (boolean (some mentions-recur? form))))\n135\t    (coll? form) (boolean (some mentions-recur? form))\n136\t    :else false))\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t;; =============================================================================\n140\t;; Sequential destructuring (slice 3)\n141\t;; =============================================================================\n142\t;;\n143\t;; A destructuring pattern lowers to ordinary symbol bindings over one\n144\t;; evaluated temporary, walked with the VM's total primitives first/rest/\n145\t;; empty? (the data module's `nth` is vector-only and refuses a list, but\n146\t;; LaTTe terms are lists):\n147\t;;\n148\t;;   [a b & r :as w] against t\n149\t;;   =>  a (first t)    c1 (rest t)\n150\t;;       b (first c1)   c2 (rest c1)\n151\t;;       r (if (empty? c2) nil c2)                        ; nthnext\n152\t;;       w t\n153\t;;\n154\t;; A nil input, a missing element and an exhausted `&` tail all yield nil,\n155\t;; as in Clojure. A non-nil remainder is a vector, the VM `rest` contract.\n156\t;; Those primitives are bare names a local binding could shadow, so a\n157\t;; destructuring form is rejected wherever first, rest or empty? is bound\n158\t;; locally. Under the convention, a guest rest definition uses raw data\n159\t;; cursors instead; previously stored definitions are not detectable here.\n160\t;; Generated names carry the reserved `dsg__` prefix and derive from the\n161\t;; binding's position, so lowering is deterministic.\n162\t\n163\t(def ^:private helper-names\n164\t  (set (map symbol [\"first\" \"rest\" \"empty?\"])))\n165\t\n166\t\n167\t(defn- locals\n168\t  [env]\n169\t  (::locals env #{}))\n170\t\n171\t\n172\t(defn- with-locals\n173\t  [env names]\n174\t  (when-let [hit (and (::convention env) (some #{'conj 'vec} names))]\n175\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"Binding \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n176\t                    {:names names})))\n177\t  (when (and (::invoker env) (some #{'invoke-value} names))\n178\t    (throw (ex-info \"Binding invoke-value would capture the guest collection invoker\" {:names names})))\n179\t  (assoc env ::locals (into (locals env) (remove #(= '& %)) names)))\n180\t\n181\t\n182\t(def ^:private reserved-prefix \"dsg__\")\n183\t\n184\t\n185\t(defn- reject!\n186\t  [message data]\n187\t  (throw (ex-info message data)))\n188\t\n189\t\n190\t(defn- reserved-name?\n191\t  [sym]\n192\t  (= reserved-prefix (subs (name sym) 0 (min (count (name sym))\n193\t                                             (count reserved-prefix)))))\n194\t\n195\t\n196\t(defn- check-def-name!\n197\t  \"A definition name is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix.\"\n198\t  [operator sym]\n199\t  (when-not (and (symbol? sym) (nil? (namespace sym)))\n200\t    (reject! (str operator \" needs a plain symbol name\") {:name sym}))\n201\t  (when (reserved-name? sym)\n202\t    (reject! \"Definition name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n203\t             {:name sym, :prefix reserved-prefix})))\n204\t\n205\t\n206\t(defn- check-binder!\n207\t  \"A binder is a plain symbol or a nested sequential pattern; anything else\n208\t   (maps, keywords, literals) is outside the supported surface.\"\n209\t  [b pattern]\n210\t  (cond\n211\t    (and (symbol? b) (nil? (namespace b)) (not= '& b))\n212\t    (when (reserved-name? b)\n213\t      (reject! \"Binding name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n214\t               {:binder b, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n215\t    (vector? b) nil\n216\t    (map? b) (reject! \"Map destructuring is not supported\"\n217\t                      {:binder b, :pattern pattern})\n218\t    :else (reject! \"Unsupported binding form\" {:binder b, :pattern pattern})))\n219\t\n220\t\n221\t(defn- parse-sequential-pattern\n222\t  \"Split a pattern vector into {:positional [...] :rest binder? :as sym?},\n223\t   rejecting malformed shapes.\"\n224\t  [pattern]\n225\t  (loop [xs (seq pattern), positional [], rest-binder ::none, as-sym nil]\n226\t    (if (nil? xs)\n227\t      {:positional positional, :rest rest-binder, :as as-sym}\n228\t      (let [x (first xs)]\n229\t        (cond\n230\t          (= '& x)\n231\t          (do (when (not= ::none rest-binder)\n232\t                (reject! \"Pattern has more than one &\" {:pattern pattern}))\n233\t              (when (or (nil? (next xs)) (= :as (second xs)))\n234\t                (reject! \"& needs a binder\" {:pattern pattern}))\n235\t              (check-binder! (second xs) pattern)\n236\t              (recur (nnext xs) positional (second xs) as-sym))\n237\t          (= :as x)\n238\t          (let [sym (second xs)]\n239\t            (when-not (and (symbol? sym) (nil? (namespace sym)) (not= '& sym))\n240\t              (reject! \":as needs a symbol\" {:pattern pattern}))\n241\t            (check-binder! sym pattern)\n242\t            (when (nnext xs)\n243\t              (reject! \":as must be last in a pattern\" {:pattern pattern}))\n244\t            (recur nil positional rest-binder sym))\n245\t          (keyword? x)\n246\t          (reject! \"Unsupported keyword in pattern\" {:keyword x, :pattern pattern})\n247\t          :else\n248\t          (do (when (not= ::none rest-binder)\n249\t                (reject! \"Only :as may follow the & binder\" {:pattern pattern}))\n250\t              (check-binder! x pattern)\n251\t              (recur (next xs) (conj positional x) rest-binder as-sym)))))))\n252\t\n253\t\n254\t(defn- first-form\n255\t  [cursor meta-map]\n256\t  (cond-> (list 'first cursor)\n257\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n258\t\n259\t\n260\t(defn- rest-form\n261\t  [cursor meta-map env]\n262\t  ;; Parameter and loop destructuring can be emitted after outcome lowering.\n263\t  ;; Keep their cursors raw vectors even when the guest library defines rest\n264\t  ;; with the argument-vector/outcome convention.\n265\t  (cond-> (if (contains? (::defined env) 'rest)\n266\t            (list 'data/subvec (list 'vec cursor) (list 'if (list 'empty? cursor) 0 1))\n267\t            (list 'rest cursor))\n268\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n269\t\n270\t\n271\t(defn- nthnext-form\n272\t  \"Clojure's nthnext at a cursor: nil once exhausted, else the remainder.\"\n273\t  [cursor meta-map]\n274\t  (cond-> (list 'if (list 'empty? cursor) nil cursor)\n275\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n276\t\n277\t\n278\t(defn- temp-symbol\n279\t  [path meta-map]\n280\t  (cond-> (symbol (str reserved-prefix path))\n281\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n282\t\n283\t\n284\t(defn- destructure-sequential\n285\t  \"Flat [sym form ...] bindings destructuring `pattern` against symbol `t`.\n286\t   A chain of cursors walks the value with first/rest; `path` names the\n287\t   generated temporaries so nested patterns stay distinct.\"\n288\t  [pattern t path env]\n289\t  (let [{:keys [positional rest as]} (parse-sequential-pattern pattern)\n290\t        m (meta pattern)\n291\t        n (count positional)\n292\t        cursor (fn [i] (if (zero? i) t (temp-symbol (str path \"c\" i) m)))\n293\t        bind (fn [out b form sub-path]\n294\t               (if (vector? b)\n295\t                 (let [sub (temp-symbol sub-path (meta b))]\n296\t                   (-> out (conj sub form) (into (destructure-sequential b sub sub-path env))))\n297\t                 (conj out b form)))\n298\t        out (reduce (fn [out [i b]]\n299\t                      (cond-> (bind out b (first-form (cursor i) m) (str path \"_\" i))\n300\t                        (or (< (inc i) n) (not= ::none rest))\n301\t                        (conj (cursor (inc i)) (rest-form (cursor i) m env))))\n302\t                    []\n303\t                    (map-indexed vector positional))\n304\t        out (if (= ::none rest)\n305\t              out\n306\t              (bind out rest (nthnext-form (cursor n) m) (str path \"_r\")))]\n307\t    (cond-> out\n308\t      as (conj as t))))\n309\t\n310\t\n311\t(defn- expand-bindings\n312\t  \"Rewrite a let binding vector so every target is a plain symbol: each\n313\t   pattern becomes a temporary bound to its initializer, then the\n314\t   destructuring bindings. Initializers keep their position, so earlier\n315\t   bindings stay visible to later ones.\"\n316\t  [bindings env]\n317\t  (when-not (even? (count bindings))\n318\t    (reject! \"let requires an even number of forms in binding vector\"\n319\t             {:bindings bindings}))\n320\t  (loop [pairs (partition 2 bindings), k 0, out [], bound (locals env)]\n321\t    (if (empty? pairs)\n322\t      out\n323\t      (let [[target init] (first pairs)]\n324\t        (cond\n325\t          (and (symbol? target) (nil? (namespace target)))\n326\t          (do (check-binder! target target)\n327\t              (recur (rest pairs) (inc k) (conj out target init)\n328\t                     (conj bound target)))\n329\t          (vector? target)\n330\t          (let [temp (temp-symbol k (meta target))\n331\t                generated (destructure-sequential target temp (str k) env)\n332\t                bound' (into bound (take-nth 2) generated)]\n333\t            (when-let [hit (first (filter helper-names bound'))]\n334\t              (reject! \"Destructuring would be captured by a local binding\"\n335\t                       {:binder hit, :pattern target}))\n336\t            (recur (rest pairs) (inc k)\n337\t                   (-> out (conj temp init) (into generated))\n338\t                   bound'))\n339\t          :else (check-binder! target target))))))\n340\t\n341\t\n342\t(defn- lower-fn-params\n343\t  \"Split fn params into fresh simple binders plus the let bindings that\n344\t   destructure them. Variadic `&` at the top level is unsupported.\"\n345\t  [params]\n346\t  (when-not (vector? params)\n347\t    (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params params}))\n348\t  (reduce (fn [acc [i p]]\n349\t            (when (= '& p)\n350\t              (reject! \"Variadic fn parameters are not supported\" {:params params}))\n351\t            (check-binder! p params)\n352\t            (if (vector? p)\n353\t              (let [fresh (temp-symbol (str \"p\" i) (meta p))]\n354\t                (-> acc\n355\t                    (update :params conj fresh)\n356\t                    (update :bindings conj p fresh)))\n357\t              (update acc :params conj p)))\n358\t          {:params [], :bindings []}\n359\t          (map-indexed vector params)))\n360\t\n361\t\n362\t;; =============================================================================\n363\t;; defn headers\n364\t;; =============================================================================\n365\t\n366\t(defn- parse-head\n367\t  \"Split (op name doc? attr-map? & more) into {:name :doc :attrs :more}. A\n368\t   string or map only counts as header when a form follows it.\"\n369\t  [operator operands]\n370\t  (let [[fn-name & more] operands\n371\t        _ (check-def-name! operator fn-name)\n372\t        [doc more] (if (and (string? (first more)) (next more))\n373\t                     [(first more) (rest more)]\n374\t                     [nil more])\n375\t        [attrs more] (if (and (map? (first more)) (next more))\n376\t                       [(first more) (rest more)]\n377\t                       [nil more])]\n378\t    {:name fn-name, :doc doc, :attrs attrs, :more more}))\n379\t\n380\t\n381\t(defn- parse-defn\n382\t  \"Parse (defn name doc? attr-map? [params] body*) or\n383\t   (defn name doc? attr-map? ([params] body*)+ attr-map?). Returns\n384\t   {:name :meta :arities [{:params :body}]}. Metadata accumulates as\n385\t   Clojure's defn does: name meta (with defn-'s :private), then the\n386\t   docstring, the attr-map and the trailing attr-map, later ones winning.\"\n387\t  [operator operands]\n388\t  (let [{fn-name :name, :keys [doc attrs more]} (parse-head operator operands)\n389\t        header (merge (cond-> (meta fn-name)\n390\t                        (= 'defn- operator) (assoc :private true))\n391\t                      (when doc {:doc doc})\n392\t                      attrs)]\n393\t    (cond\n394\t      (vector? (first more))\n395\t      {:name fn-name, :meta header\n396\t       :arities [{:params (first more), :body (rest more)}]}\n397\t\n398\t      (and (seq? (first more)) (vector? (ffirst more)))\n399\t      (let [arities (take-while seq? more)\n400\t            trailing (drop (count arities) more)]\n401\t        (when (and (seq trailing)\n402\t                   (not (and (map? (first trailing)) (nil? (next trailing)))))\n403\t          (reject! \"Unexpected forms after fn arities\" {:name fn-name}))\n404\t        {:name fn-name, :meta (merge header (first trailing))\n405\t         :arities (mapv (fn [a]\n406\t                          (when-not (vector? (first a))\n407\t                            (reject! \"Malformed fn arity\" {:name fn-name}))\n408\t                          {:params (first a), :body (rest a)})\n409\t                        arities)})\n410\t\n411\t      :else\n412\t      (reject! (str \"Malformed \" operator \" form\") {:name fn-name}))))\n413\t\n414\t\n415\t(declare compile-fn compile-av-fn)\n416\t\n417\t\n418\t(defn- compile-defn\n419\t  \"Compile a defn form natively to a yin/def application: the tree the\n420\t   expander's standard `defn` also produces. This path is used only when no\n421\t   defmacro named defn is in scope. Several arities need the argument-vector\n422\t   convention: a plain Yin closure nil-fills missing arguments and drops\n423\t   extras, so it cannot observe the call's argument count.\"\n424\t  [operator operands env tail? macro-env]\n425\t  (let [{fn-name :name, header :meta, :keys [arities]} (parse-defn operator operands)\n426\t        fn-ast (if (::convention env)\n427\t                 (compile-av-fn arities env false macro-env fn-name)\n428\t                 (do (when (< 1 (count arities))\n429\t                       (reject! \"Multi-arity fn is not supported: closures cannot observe argument count\"\n430\t                                {:name fn-name, :arities (count arities)}))\n431\t                     (let [{:keys [params body]} (first arities)]\n432\t                       (compile-fn params body env false macro-env))))\n433\t        ast (cond-> {:type :application\n434\t                     :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def}\n435\t                     :operands [{:type :literal, :value (strip-symbol-meta fn-name)}\n436\t                                fn-ast]}\n437\t              tail? (assoc :tail? true))]\n438\t    (if (seq header)\n439\t      (vary-meta ast merge header)\n440\t      ast)))\n441\t\n442\t\n443\t(defn- check-macro-params!\n444\t  \"Every macro parameter is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix; an\n445\t   & must be followed by exactly one binder.\"\n446\t  [params]\n447\t  (doseq [p params :when (not= '& p)]\n448\t    (check-binder! p params)\n449\t    (when-not (symbol? p)\n450\t      (reject! \"defmacro parameters must be plain symbols\" {:params params})))\n451\t  (when-let [i (first (keep-indexed (fn [i p] (when (= '& p) i)) params))]\n452\t    (when-not (= (+ i 2) (count params))\n453\t      (reject! \"& needs exactly one binder in defmacro parameters\" {:params params}))))\n454\t\n455\t\n456\t(defn- compile-defmacro\n457\t  \"Lower (defmacro name doc? attr-map? [params] body*) to ordinary\n458\t   (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax. The lambda is flagged `:macro?` for the\n459\t   encoder's declaration row (yin.vm.macro.md §10.2); projection drops the\n460\t   flag from the row.\"\n461\t  [operands env tail? macro-env]\n462\t  (let [{fn-name :name, :keys [doc attrs more]} (parse-head 'defmacro operands)\n463\t        params (first more)\n464\t        _ (when-not (vector? params)\n465\t            (reject! \"defmacro needs a parameter vector\" {:name fn-name}))\n466\t        _ (check-macro-params! params)\n467\t        header (merge (when doc {:doc doc}) attrs)\n468\t        ast (cond-> {:type :application\n469\t                     :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def}\n470\t                     :operands [{:type :literal, :value (strip-symbol-meta fn-name)}\n471\t                                (assoc (compile-lambda params (body-expression (rest more))\n472\t                                                       env false macro-env)\n473\t                                       :macro? true)]}\n474\t              tail? (assoc :tail? true))]\n475\t    (if (seq header)\n476\t      (vary-meta ast merge header)\n477\t      ast)))\n478\t\n479\t\n480\t(defn special-form?\n481\t  \"Check if a form is a special form.\"\n482\t  [form]\n483\t  (and (seq? form)\n484\t       (symbol? (first form))\n485\t       (contains? #{'fn 'if 'let 'quote 'do 'def 'dao.stream.apply/call 'defmacro 'loop 'recur} (first form))))\n486\t\n487\t\n488\t(defn compile-literal\n489\t  \"Compile a literal value to Universal AST.\"\n490\t  [form _tail?]\n491\t  {:type :literal, :value form})\n492\t\n493\t\n494\t(defn compile-variable\n495\t  \"Compile a variable reference (symbol) to Universal AST.\"\n496\t  [sym _tail?]\n497\t  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n498\t\n499\t\n500\t(defn compile-def\n501\t  \"Compile a def form to Universal AST.\n502\t   Emits a yin/def application which requires environment support.\"\n503\t  ([sym value env tail?] (compile-def sym value env tail? initial-macro-env))\n504\t  ([sym value env tail? macro-env]\n505\t   (check-def-name! 'def sym)\n506\t   (cond-> {:type :application,\n507\t            :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def},\n508\t            :operands [{:type :literal, :value sym}\n509\t                       (compile-form value false env macro-env)]}\n510\t     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n511\t\n512\t\n513\t(defn compile-lambda\n514\t  \"Compile a lambda (fn) expression to Universal AST.\n515\t\n516\t  Clojure: (fn [x y] (+ x y))\n517\t  AST: {:type :lambda\n518\t        :params [x y]\n519\t        :body <compiled-body>}\"\n520\t  ([params body env tail?] (compile-lambda params body env tail? initial-macro-env))\n521\t  ([params body env tail? macro-env]\n522\t   (let [new-macro-env (shadow-macro-env macro-env params)\n523\t         ;; a source fn boundary resets the recur target\n524\t         compiled-body (compile-form body true\n525\t                                     (with-locals (dissoc env ::target) params)\n526\t                                     new-macro-env)]\n527\t     (cond-> {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body compiled-body}\n528\t       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n529\t\n530\t\n531\t(defn- compile-fn\n532\t  \"Compile (fn [params] body*) where params may hold sequential patterns:\n533\t   each pattern parameter becomes a fresh simple binder, and the body is\n534\t   wrapped in a let that destructures it.\"\n535\t  [params body-forms env tail? macro-env]\n536\t  (let [{simple :params, bindings :bindings} (lower-fn-params params)]\n537\t    (if (some mentions-recur? body-forms)\n538\t      ;; function-level recur: the body runs as a loop over the parameters,\n539\t      ;; so a pattern parameter re-destructures on every iteration\n540\t      (compile-lambda simple\n541\t                      (with-meta (list* 'loop (vec (interleave params simple)) body-forms)\n542\t                        {::fn-loop true})\n543\t                      env tail? macro-env)\n544\t      (let [body (body-expression body-forms)]\n545\t        (compile-lambda simple\n546\t                        (if (seq bindings) (list 'let bindings body) body)\n547\t                        env tail? macro-env)))))\n548\t\n549\t\n550\t;; =============================================================================\n551\t;; Argument-vector convention (slice 3b)\n552\t;; =============================================================================\n553\t;;\n554\t;; A Yin closure nil-fills missing arguments and drops extras, so a guest\n555\t;; closure cannot observe its call's argument count. Opted in at\n556\t;; `compile-program` (`:convention :arg-vector`), every user fn and defn\n557\t;; instead becomes ONE closure taking ONE vector, branching on its count:\n558\t;;\n559\t;;   (fn ([a] e1) ([a b] e2))\n560\t;;   =>  (fn [dsg__av]\n561\t;;         (if (data/content= (data/count dsg__av) 1)\n562\t;;           (let [a (data/nth dsg__av 0)] e1)\n563\t;;           (if (data/content= (data/count dsg__av) 2)\n564\t;;             (let [a (data/nth dsg__av 0) b (data/nth dsg__av 1)] e2)\n565\t;;             (data/count))))                     ; refused: no such arity\n566\t;;\n567\t;; The dispatch names are module-qualified, which no let binder can shadow.\n568\t;; A call is (f (conj [] a b)) in tail position when the operator is not\n569\t;; statically native; a native name (a primitive or module export, not bound\n570\t;; locally and not defined by the program) is called directly, and in value\n571\t;; position becomes a fresh adapter closure over the same convention. The\n572\t;; program's own macro names stay ordinary applications: the expander\n573\t;; recognizes those calls, so their operands must stay ordinary.\n574\t\n575\t(def ^:private av-sym (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"av\")))\n576\t\n577\t\n578\t(def ^:private default-adapter-arity\n579\t  \"The largest count an adapter admits for a native name with no declared\n580\t   profile (`:native` given as a plain set).\"\n581\t  4)\n582\t\n583\t\n584\t(def ^:private adapter-variadic-cap\n585\t  \"How far an adapter extends a `:variadic` profile arity: an adapter is a\n586\t   finite dispatch, so an open-ended arity needs a stated bound.\"\n587\t  8)\n588\t\n589\t\n590\t(defn- native-name?\n591\t  \"True when `sym` statically names a primitive or host-module export.\"\n592\t  [env sym]\n593\t  (when-let [conv (::convention env)]\n594\t    (and (symbol? sym)\n595\t         (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n596\t         (not (contains? (::defined env) sym))\n597\t         (or (some? (namespace sym))\n598\t             (contains? (:native conv) sym)))))\n599\t\n600\t\n601\t(defn- macro-call?\n602\t  [env macro-env sym]\n603\t  (and (symbol? sym)\n604\t       (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n605\t       (or (contains? macro-env sym)\n606\t           (contains? (:macros (::convention env)) sym))))\n607\t\n608\t\n609\t;; =============================================================================\n610\t;; Outcome model (slice 5)\n611\t;; =============================================================================\n612\t;;\n613\t;; Opted in with `:outcomes true` beside the argument-vector convention. Every\n614\t;; guest function then returns an outcome, a tagged two-element vector:\n615\t;;\n616\t;;   [:yin.k/ok value]       success; a LaTTe [:ok ...] stays an ordinary value\n617\t;;   [:yin.k/error data]     failure; never a truthy return, only ever consumed\n618\t;;                           by a call-site test or the harness boundary\n619\t;;\n620\t;; Lowering is a source-to-source pass over one function body, run before the\n621\t;; ordinary compile. A tail form returns an outcome: a value is wrapped,\n622\t;; and a source call is admitted before invoking the common entry. Generated\n623\t;; entries can forward a private body's outcome directly in tail position;\n624\t;; public entries convert value/raise through the caller bridge. This keeps\n625\t;; named and mutual tail chains at constant depth. `throw` becomes the error\n626\t;; outcome. A may-fail form in operand position is the early return pattern:\n627\t;;\n628\t;;   (let [o <outcome>] (if (error? o) o <rest of the function with (payload o)>))\n629\t;;\n630\t;; The failing branch returns the outcome in tail position. `ex-info` becomes\n631\t;; a portable map under namespaced keys. A native primitive returns a raw\n632\t;; value, except an adapted one (`:adapters`, source symbol to adapter symbol),\n633\t;; whose host adapter already returns an outcome. Generated names carry the\n634\t;; reserved `dsg__` prefix and bind through the internal `dsg__let`, which\n635\t;; skips the user-binder check; the program pre-pass keeps user code out of\n636\t;; that prefix. A macro call is opaque to the pass: the expander owns it.\n637\t\n638\t(def ^:private ok-tag :yin.k/ok)\n639\t\n640\t(def ^:private error-tag :yin.k/error)\n641\t\n642\t\n643\t(defn- outcomes?\n644\t  [env]\n645\t  (some? (::outcomes env)))\n646\t\n647\t\n648\t(defn- adapters\n649\t  [env]\n650\t  (:adapters (::outcomes env)))\n651\t\n652\t\n653\t(defn- binder-symbols\n654\t  [b]\n655\t  (into #{} (comp (filter symbol?) (remove #{'&})) (tree-seq coll? seq b)))\n656\t\n657\t\n658\t(defn- ok-form\n659\t  [v]\n660\t  [ok-tag v])\n661\t\n662\t\n663\t(defn- rebuild\n664\t  \"A list of `items` carrying the reader metadata of `form`.\"\n665\t  [form items]\n666\t  (let [out (apply list items)]\n667\t    (if-let [m (meta form)]\n668\t      (with-meta out m)\n669\t      out)))\n670\t\n671\t\n672\t(defn- gen-sym\n673\t  [env]\n674\t  (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"o\" (swap! (::gen env) inc))))\n675\t\n676\t\n677\t(defn- rewrite-ex-info\n678\t  \"(ex-info msg data cause?) as the portable map holding its parts.\"\n679\t  [form]\n680\t  (cond\n681\t    (seq? form)\n682\t    (cond\n683\t      (empty? form) form\n684\t      (= 'quote (first form)) form\n685\t      (#{'.getMessage 'ex-message 'ex-data} (first form))\n686\t      (do (when-not (= 2 (count form))\n687\t            (reject! \"Error accessor requires one portable error value\" {:form form}))\n688\t          (list (if (= 'ex-data (first form)) :yin.k/data :yin.k/message)\n689\t                (rewrite-ex-info (second form))))\n690\t      (and (symbol? (first form)) (= \\. (first (name (first form)))))\n691\t      (reject! \"Host exception/interop accessor is not portable\" {:form form})\n692\t      (= 'ex-info (first form))\n693\t      (let [[_ msg data cause] (map rewrite-ex-info form)]\n694\t        (cond-> {:yin.k/message msg, :yin.k/data data}\n695\t          (< 3 (count form)) (assoc :yin.k/cause cause)))\n696\t      :else (rebuild form (map rewrite-ex-info form)))\n697\t    (vector? form) (with-meta (mapv rewrite-ex-info form) (meta form))\n698\t    (map? form) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(rewrite-ex-info k) (rewrite-ex-info v)])) form)\n699\t    (set? form) (into #{} (map rewrite-ex-info) form)\n700\t    :else form))\n701\t\n702\t\n703\t(defn- call-kind\n704\t  [env head]\n705\t  (cond\n706\t    (keyword? head) :keyword\n707\t    (not (symbol? head)) :guest\n708\t    (macro-call? env (::macro-env env) head) :macro\n709\t    (native-name? env head) (if (contains? (adapters env) head) :adapted :native)\n710\t    :else :guest))\n711\t\n712\t\n713\t(def ^:private lowered-specials\n714\t  #{'if 'let 'do 'loop 'recur 'throw 'try 'quote 'fn 'and 'or})\n715\t\n716\t\n717\t(declare failing? expand-control)\n718\t\n719\t\n720\t(def ^:private control-heads\n721\t  \"case and the standard control forms: compiler forms that lower to\n722\t   if/let/do, so the outcome pass sees through them like those.\"\n723\t  #{'case 'cond 'when 'if-let 'if-some 'when-let 'when-some '->})\n724\t\n725\t\n726\t(defn- any-failing?\n727\t  [env forms]\n728\t  (boolean (some #(failing? env %) forms)))\n729\t\n730\t\n731\t(defn- check-macro-operands!\n732\t  \"A macro call is opaque to the lowering pass, so an operand that may fail\n733\t   would escape the early return: refuse it, naming the macro.\"\n734\t  [env head ops]\n735\t  (when (any-failing? env ops)\n736\t    (reject! (str \"Macro call \" head \" has an operand that may fail; \"\n737\t                  \"the outcome model cannot lower it\")\n738\t             {:macro head})))\n739\t\n740\t\n741\t(defn- scoped-failing?\n742\t  \"Whether a sequence of [target init] pairs or the body after them can fail,\n743\t   each init seeing the targets before it.\"\n744\t  [env pairs body]\n745\t  (loop [env env, ps pairs]\n746\t    (if (empty? ps)\n747\t      (any-failing? env body)\n748\t      (let [[target init] (first ps)]\n749\t        (or (failing? env init)\n750\t            (recur (with-locals env (binder-symbols target)) (rest ps)))))))\n751\t\n752\t\n753\t(defn- failing?\n754\t  \"True when evaluating `form` can produce an error outcome: a throw, or a\n755\t   call that returns an outcome (a guest call or an adapted primitive).\"\n756\t  [env form]\n757\t  (cond\n758\t    (seq? form)\n759\t    (if (empty? form)\n760\t      false\n761\t      (let [[head & ops] form]\n762\t        (cond\n763\t          (contains? #{'quote 'fn} head) false\n764\t          (= 'throw head) true\n765\t          (= 'try head) true\n766\t          (= 'let head) (let [[bindings & body] ops]\n767\t                          (scoped-failing? env (partition 2 (expand-bindings bindings env)) body))\n768\t          ;; the raw outcome of one guest call is a value, not a failure\n769\t          (= 'yin.k/outcome-of head) (do (when-not (and (= 1 (count ops)) (seq? (first ops)))\n770\t                                           (reject! \"yin.k/outcome-of takes one call\" {:form form}))\n771\t                                         (when (any-failing? env (first ops))\n772\t                                           (reject! \"yin.k/outcome-of operands cannot fail\"\n773\t                                                    {:form form}))\n774\t                                         false)\n775\t          (= 'dsg__let head) (let [[bindings & body] ops]\n776\t                               (scoped-failing? env (partition 2 bindings) body))\n777\t          (= 'loop head) (let [[bindings & body] ops]\n778\t                           (scoped-failing? env (partition 2 bindings) body))\n779\t          (contains? control-heads head) (failing? env (expand-control env head ops))\n780\t          (contains? lowered-specials head) (any-failing? env ops)\n781\t          :else (case (call-kind env head)\n782\t                  (:guest :adapted) true\n783\t                  :macro (do (check-macro-operands! env head ops) false)\n784\t                  (any-failing? env ops)))))\n785\t    (or (vector? form) (set? form)) (any-failing? env form)\n786\t    (map? form) (any-failing? env (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n787\t    :else false))\n788\t\n789\t\n790\t(defn- atomic?\n791\t  [form]\n792\t  (or (symbol? form) (constant-form? form)))\n793\t\n794\t\n795\t(declare lower-tail)\n796\t\n797\t\n798\t(defn- bind-outcome\n799\t  \"Bind `outcome`, return it as is when it is an error, else continue with\n800\t   its payload.\"\n801\t  [env outcome k]\n802\t  (let [o (gen-sym env)]\n803\t    (list 'dsg__let [o outcome]\n804\t          (list 'if (list 'data/content= (list 'data/nth o 0) error-tag)\n805\t                o\n806\t                (k (list 'data/nth o 1))))))\n807\t\n808\t\n809\t(defn- lower-operand\n810\t  \"Continue with a simple form for `form`: the form itself when it cannot\n811\t   fail, else the payload of its outcome.\"\n812\t  [env form k]\n813\t  (if (failing? env form)\n814\t    (bind-outcome env (lower-tail env form) k)\n815\t    (k form)))\n816\t\n817\t\n818\t(defn- lower-operands\n819\t  \"Continue with simple forms for `forms`, evaluated left to right: a form\n820\t   before a may-fail one is bound first so the order of effects survives.\"\n821\t  [env forms k]\n822\t  (letfn [(go\n823\t            [fs acc]\n824\t            (if (empty? fs)\n825\t              (k acc)\n826\t              (let [f (first fs), more (rest fs)]\n827\t                (cond\n828\t                  (atomic? f) (go more (conj acc f))\n829\t                  (failing? env f) (lower-operand env f (fn [v] (go more (conj acc v))))\n830\t                  (any-failing? env more) (let [t (gen-sym env)]\n831\t                                            (list 'dsg__let [t f] (go more (conj acc t))))\n832\t                  :else (go more (conj acc f))))))]\n833\t    (go (seq forms) [])))\n834\t\n835\t\n836\t(defn- lower-let\n837\t  \"`pairs` are plain [symbol init] pairs.\"\n838\t  [env pairs body]\n839\t  (letfn [(go\n840\t            [env ps]\n841\t            (if (empty? ps)\n842\t              (lower-tail env (body-expression body))\n843\t              (let [[x init] (first ps)]\n844\t                (lower-operand env init\n845\t                               (fn [v]\n846\t                                 (list 'dsg__let [x v]\n847\t                                       (go (with-locals env [x]) (rest ps))))))))]\n848\t    (go env pairs)))\n849\t\n850\t\n851\t(defn- lower-loop\n852\t  [env bindings body]\n853\t  (when-not (and (vector? bindings) (even? (count bindings)))\n854\t    (reject! \"loop requires an even-sized binding vector\" {:bindings bindings}))\n855\t  (let [pairs (partition 2 bindings)\n856\t        targets (map first pairs)]\n857\t    (if (scoped-failing? env pairs nil)\n858\t      ;; a may-fail initializer: bind outside, loop over the plain names\n859\t      (do (when-not (every? symbol? targets)\n860\t            (reject! \"A pattern loop binder cannot have a may-fail initializer\"\n861\t                     {:bindings bindings}))\n862\t          (lower-tail env (list 'let bindings\n863\t                                (list 'loop (vec (mapcat (fn [t] [t t]) targets))\n864\t                                      (body-expression body)))))\n865\t      (list 'loop bindings\n866\t            (lower-tail (with-locals env (mapcat binder-symbols targets))\n867\t                        (body-expression body))))))\n868\t\n869\t\n870\t(defn- lower-tail\n871\t  \"The form whose value is the outcome of evaluating `form` in tail position.\"\n872\t  [env form]\n873\t  (cond\n874\t    (seq? form)\n875\t    (if (empty? form)\n876\t      (ok-form form)\n877\t      (let [[head & ops] form]\n878\t        (case (when (symbol? head) head)\n879\t          if (let [[t c & more] ops]\n880\t               (lower-operand env t\n881\t                              (fn [tv]\n882\t                                (list 'if tv (lower-tail env c)\n883\t                                      (if (seq more)\n884\t                                        (lower-tail env (first more))\n885\t                                        (ok-form nil))))))\n886\t          let (do (when-not (vector? (first ops))\n887\t                    (reject! \"let requires a binding vector\" {:bindings (first ops)}))\n888\t                  (lower-let env (partition 2 (expand-bindings (first ops) env)) (rest ops)))\n889\t          dsg__let (lower-let env (partition 2 (first ops)) (rest ops))\n890\t          do (case (count ops)\n891\t               0 (ok-form nil)\n892\t               1 (lower-tail env (first ops))\n893\t               (lower-operand env (first ops)\n894\t                              (fn [v] (list 'do v (lower-tail env (cons 'do (rest ops)))))))\n895\t          loop (lower-loop env (first ops) (rest ops))\n896\t          recur (lower-operands env (vec ops) (fn [vs] (rebuild form (cons 'recur vs))))\n897\t          throw (lower-operand env (first ops) (fn [v] [error-tag v]))\n898\t          try (let [clauses (filter #(and (seq? %) (#{'catch 'finally} (first %))) ops)\n899\t                    body (take-while #(not (and (seq? %) (#{'catch 'finally} (first %)))) ops)\n900\t                    [clause] clauses\n901\t                    [_ klass binding & handler] clause\n902\t                    outcome (gen-sym env)]\n903\t                (when-not (and (= (count ops) (+ (count body) (count clauses)))\n904\t                               (= 1 (count clauses)) (= 'catch (first clause))\n905\t                               (#{'Exception 'java.lang.Exception\n906\t                                  'clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo} klass)\n907\t                               (symbol? binding))\n908\t                  (reject! \"Portable try requires one Exception/ExceptionInfo catch and no finally\"\n909\t                           {:form form :clauses clauses}))\n910\t                (check-binder! binding clause)\n911\t                (list 'dsg__let [outcome (lower-tail env (body-expression body))]\n912\t                      (list 'if (list 'data/content= (list 'data/nth outcome 0) error-tag)\n913\t                            (list 'dsg__let [binding (list 'data/nth outcome 1)]\n914\t                                  (lower-tail (with-locals env [binding]) (body-expression handler)))\n915\t                            outcome)))\n916\t          (quote fn) (ok-form form)\n917\t          (case cond when if-let if-some when-let when-some ->)\n918\t          (lower-tail env (expand-control env head ops))\n919\t          and (case (count ops)\n920\t                0 (ok-form true)\n921\t                1 (lower-tail env (first ops))\n922\t                (let [g (gen-sym env)]\n923\t                  (lower-tail env (list 'dsg__let [g (first ops)]\n924\t                                        (list 'if g (cons 'and (rest ops)) g)))))\n925\t          or (case (count ops)\n926\t               0 (ok-form nil)\n927\t               1 (lower-tail env (first ops))\n928\t               (let [g (gen-sym env)]\n929\t                 (lower-tail env (list 'dsg__let [g (first ops)]\n930\t                                       (list 'if g g (cons 'or (rest ops)))))))\n931\t          (case (call-kind env head)\n932\t            :macro (do (check-macro-operands! env head ops) (ok-form form))\n933\t            :keyword (lower-operands env (vec ops)\n934\t                                     (fn [vs] (ok-form (rebuild form (cons head vs)))))\n935\t            :native (lower-operands env (vec ops)\n936\t                                    (fn [vs] (ok-form (rebuild form (cons head vs)))))\n937\t            :adapted (lower-operands env (vec ops)\n938\t                                     (fn [vs] (rebuild form (cons (get (adapters env) head) vs))))\n939\t            :guest (lower-operands env (into [head] ops)\n940\t                                   (fn [vs] (rebuild form vs)))))))\n941\t    (or (vector? form) (set? form) (map? form))\n942\t    (if (failing? env form)\n943\t      (cond\n944\t        (vector? form) (lower-operands env form (fn [vs] (ok-form (vec vs))))\n945\t        (set? form) (lower-operands env (vec form) (fn [vs] (ok-form (set vs))))\n946\t        :else (lower-operands env (vec (mapcat identity form))\n947\t                              (fn [vs] (ok-form (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 vs))))))\n948\t      (ok-form form))\n949\t    :else (ok-form form)))\n950\t\n951\t\n952\t(defn- lower-function-body\n953\t  \"The outcome-returning body of one function over `params`.\"\n954\t  [env macro-env params body-forms]\n955\t  (lower-tail (-> env\n956\t                  (assoc ::macro-env macro-env, ::gen (atom 0))\n957\t                  (with-locals (mapcat binder-symbols params)))\n958\t              (rewrite-ex-info (body-expression body-forms))))\n959\t\n960\t\n961\t(def ^:private source-keys [:line :column :end-line :end-column])\n962\t\n963\t\n964\t(defn- source-meta\n965\t  \"The source position keys of `form`'s reader metadata, or nil.\"\n966\t  [form]\n967\t  (not-empty (select-keys (meta form) source-keys)))\n968\t\n969\t\n970\t(defn- arity-error-form\n971\t  \"The outcome of a call whose argument count no arity admits: it names the\n972\t   function, never a zero-argument data/count refusal naming count. An\n973\t   anonymous fn has no name: it is `:yin.k/kind :anonymous` and carries the\n974\t   fn form's source position, when the reader gave one.\"\n975\t  [fn-name source]\n976\t  [error-tag (cond-> {:yin.vm.data/reason :arity\n977\t                      :yin.k/argc (list 'data/count av-sym)}\n978\t               fn-name (assoc :yin.k/fn (list 'quote fn-name))\n979\t               (nil? fn-name) (assoc :yin.k/kind :anonymous)\n980\t               (and (nil? fn-name) source) (assoc :yin.k/source source))])\n981\t\n982\t\n983\t(defn outcome-adapter\n984\t  \"Wrap host function `f`, a primitive declaring domain failures, as an\n985\t   outcome-returning one: success is [:yin.k/ok value], and the module's own\n986\t   refusal (ex-info with message `refusal-message` and :yin.vm.data/op and\n987\t   :yin.vm.data/reason in its data) is [:yin.k/error data] with those keys.\n988\t   Any other host exception propagates: an unexpected VM or compiler failure\n989\t   is never a successful rejection.\"\n990\t  [refusal-message f]\n991\t  (fn [& args]\n992\t    (try\n993\t      [ok-tag (apply f args)]\n994\t      (catch #?(:clj Throwable, :cljs :default, :cljd Object) e\n995\t        (let [data (ex-data e)]\n996\t          (if (and (= refusal-message (ex-message e))\n997\t                   (contains? data :yin.vm.data/op)\n998\t                   (contains? data :yin.vm.data/reason))\n999\t            [error-tag data]\n1000\t            (throw e)))))))\n1001\t\n1002\t\n1003\t(defn- av-let\n1004\t  \"(let [p0 (data/nth av 0) ...] body): positional parameters of one arity.\n1005\t   A body that recurs is a loop over the same bindings: one recur target per\n1006\t   arity. Under the outcome model the body is lowered first.\"\n1007\t  [env macro-env params body-forms]\n1008\t  (let [bindings (into [] (mapcat (fn [i p] [p (list 'data/nth av-sym i)]) (range) params))\n1009\t        lowered? (outcomes? env)\n1010\t        body (if lowered?\n1011\t               (lower-function-body env macro-env params body-forms)\n1012\t               (body-expression body-forms))]\n1013\t    (if (some mentions-recur? body-forms)\n1014\t      (with-meta (if lowered?\n1015\t                   (list 'loop bindings body)\n1016\t                   (list* 'loop bindings body-forms))\n1017\t        {::fn-loop true})\n1018\t      (list 'let bindings body))))\n1019\t\n1020\t\n1021\t(defn- av-dispatch\n1022\t  \"Nested ifs over the argument vector's count, one branch per arity\n1023\t   {:n count :form branch}. An unmatched count falls through to a\n1024\t   zero-argument data/count, which the data module refuses with :reason\n1025\t   :arity; under the outcome model it is an arity error outcome naming\n1026\t   `fn-name` (or the anonymous fn's `source`) instead.\"\n1027\t  [env fn-name source arities]\n1028\t  (let [counts (map :n arities)]\n1029\t    (when (not= (count counts) (count (set counts)))\n1030\t      (reject! \"Two arities with the same parameter count\" {:counts (vec counts)}))\n1031\t    (reduce (fn [else {:keys [n form]}]\n1032\t              (list 'if\n1033\t                    (list 'data/content= (list 'data/count av-sym) n)\n1034\t                    form\n1035\t                    else))\n1036\t            (if (outcomes? env) (arity-error-form fn-name source) (list 'data/count))\n1037\t            (reverse arities))))\n1038\t\n1039\t\n1040\t(defn- check-av-params!\n1041\t  [params]\n1042\t  (when-not (vector? params)\n1043\t    (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params params}))\n1044\t  (doseq [p params]\n1045\t    (when (= '& p)\n1046\t      (reject! \"Variadic fn parameters are not supported\" {:params params}))\n1047\t    (check-binder! p params)))\n1048\t\n1049\t\n1050\t(defn- outcome-node\n1051\t  [tag value]\n1052\t  (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/lit tag)) value))\n1053\t\n1054\t\n1055\t(defn- call-entry\n1056\t  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body.\"\n1057\t  []\n1058\t  (let [body (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"body\"))\n1059\t        invocation (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invocation\"))\n1060\t        outcome (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"entry_outcome\"))\n1061\t        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n1062\t        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n1063\t        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1064\t        binding-error (outcome-node\n1065\t                        error-tag\n1066\t                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1067\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n1068\t                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n1069\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n1070\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1071\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n1072\t        entry-body (u/let1\n1073\t                     outcome\n1074\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1075\t                                (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1076\t                                binding-error)\n1077\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1078\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 0))\n1079\t                                       (u/lit ok-tag))\n1080\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))\n1081\t                                (u/app raise\n1082\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown)\n1083\t                                              (u/app (u/v 'data/nth)\n1084\t                                                     (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))))))\n1085\t        ;; The private lane forwards the body's outcome in tail position.\n1086\t        ;; The public entry still converts outcomes to value/raise normally.\n1087\t        entry (u/lam [invocation]\n1088\t                     (u/if-node\n1089\t                       (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1090\t                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation)\n1091\t                                     (u/lit :clj/outcome-token))\n1092\t                              (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1093\t                       (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1094\t                                  (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1095\t                                  binding-error)\n1096\t                       entry-body))]\n1097\t    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n1098\t\n1099\t\n1100\t(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n1101\t  \"Admit a descriptor constructed by trusted UAST/profile code. This is not\n1102\t   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n1103\t  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n1104\t  (let [descriptor-name 'dsg__descriptor\n1105\t        canonical (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) descriptor-ast\n1106\t                         (u/lit :clj/admission) (u/lit nil))\n1107\t        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private\n1108\t        ;; token. Projection reconstructs and compares that opaque closure;\n1109\t        ;; it never applies a source-supplied predicate. An equal immutable\n1110\t        ;; reconstruction is the same value, not admission of different data.\n1111\t        witness (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_admission) (u/v descriptor-name))\n1112\t        published (u/let1 descriptor-name canonical\n1113\t                          (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v descriptor-name)\n1114\t                                 (u/lit :clj/admission) witness))]\n1115\t    (cond-> (u/mark-tails published)\n1116\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n1117\t\n1118\t\n1119\t(defn- compile-call-descriptor\n1120\t  \"Publish a private body through a canonical constructor-created entry.\"\n1121\t  [body-ast tail?]\n1122\t  (admit-call-descriptor\n1123\t    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1124\t           (u/lit :yang.call/entry) (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_entry) body-ast)\n1125\t           (u/lit :clj/type) (u/lit :function)\n1126\t           (u/lit :clj/outcomes?) (u/lit true))\n1127\t    tail?))\n1128\t\n1129\t\n1130\t(defn- compile-av-fn\n1131\t  \"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\n1132\t   `fn-name` names the function in an arity error outcome. Under the outcome\n1133\t   model the published value is an immutable common-call descriptor.\"\n1134\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env nil nil))\n1135\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env fn-name nil))\n1136\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name source]\n1137\t   (let [arities (mapv (fn [{:keys [params body]}]\n1138\t                         (check-av-params! params)\n1139\t                         {:n (count params)\n1140\t                          :form (av-let env macro-env params body)})\n1141\t                       arities)\n1142\t         body (compile-lambda [av-sym] (av-dispatch env fn-name source arities)\n1143\t                              env false macro-env)]\n1144\t     (if (outcomes? env)\n1145\t       (compile-call-descriptor body tail?)\n1146\t       (cond-> body tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\n1147\t\n1148\t\n1149\t(defn- fn-arities\n1150\t  \"Arities of (fn [params] body*) or (fn ([params] body*)+) operands.\"\n1151\t  [operands]\n1152\t  (cond\n1153\t    (vector? (first operands))\n1154\t    [{:params (first operands), :body (rest operands)}]\n1155\t\n1156\t    (and (seq operands) (every? #(and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) operands))\n1157\t    (mapv (fn [a] {:params (first a), :body (rest a)}) operands)\n1158\t\n1159\t    :else (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params (first operands)})))\n1160\t\n1161\t\n1162\t(defn- adapter-counts\n1163\t  \"The argument counts an adapter for native `sym` admits: the fixed arities\n1164\t   of its `:yin.k/arities` profile, extended to `adapter-variadic-cap` when\n1165\t   the profile is `:variadic`. A name with no declared profile admits\n1166\t   0 to `default-adapter-arity`.\"\n1167\t  [env sym]\n1168\t  (if-let [declared (get-in env [::convention :arities sym])]\n1169\t    (let [fixed (filter number? declared)\n1170\t          from (if (seq fixed) (apply max fixed) 0)]\n1171\t      (vec (sort (distinct (concat fixed\n1172\t                                   (when (some #{:variadic} declared)\n1173\t                                     (range from (inc (max from adapter-variadic-cap)))))))))\n1174\t    (vec (range (inc default-adapter-arity)))))\n1175\t\n1176\t\n1177\t(defn- compile-adapter\n1178\t  \"A fresh closure over the convention that calls native `sym` with the\n1179\t   unpacked arguments, for each admitted count.\"\n1180\t  [sym env tail? macro-env]\n1181\t  (let [arities (mapv (fn [n]\n1182\t                        (let [call (cons sym (map #(list 'data/nth av-sym %) (range n)))]\n1183\t                          {:n n\n1184\t                           :form (if (outcomes? env)\n1185\t                                   (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [call])\n1186\t                                   call)}))\n1187\t                      (adapter-counts env sym))]\n1188\t    (compile-lambda [av-sym] (av-dispatch env sym nil arities) env tail? macro-env)))\n1189\t\n1190\t\n1191\t(defn- apply-call?\n1192\t  \"True when `operator` is the `apply` intrinsic: not bound locally and not\n1193\t   defined by the program.\"\n1194\t  [env operator]\n1195\t  (and (= 'apply operator)\n1196\t       (not (contains? (locals env) operator))\n1197\t       (not (contains? (::defined env) operator))))\n1198\t\n1199\t\n1200\t(defn- compile-guest-call\n1201\t  \"Admit a source operator before common invocation. Only generated UAST\n1202\t   implementation calls apply private closures directly.\"\n1203\t  [callee-ast arguments-ast env tail?]\n1204\t  (if-not (outcomes? env)\n1205\t    (cond-> (u/app callee-ast arguments-ast)\n1206\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n1207\t    (let [callee (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"callee\"))\n1208\t          arguments (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"arguments\"))\n1209\t          escape (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"raise_escape\"))\n1210\t          condition (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"condition\"))\n1211\t          result (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"call_result\"))\n1212\t          condition->outcome (u/if-node\n1213\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1214\t                                      (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n1215\t                                             (u/lit :yang.call/reason))\n1216\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/thrown))\n1217\t                               (outcome-node\n1218\t                                 error-tag\n1219\t                                 (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n1220\t                                        (u/lit :yang.call/value)))\n1221\t                               (outcome-node error-tag (u/v condition)))\n1222\t          raise (u/lam [condition]\n1223\t                       (assoc (u/app (u/v escape)\n1224\t                                     (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1225\t                                            (u/lit :clj/escape-token) (u/v 'dsg__call_token)\n1226\t                                            (u/lit :clj/outcome) condition->outcome))\n1227\t                              :tail? true))\n1228\t          common-call (u/let1\n1229\t                        result\n1230\t                        (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/invoke) (u/v callee) (u/v arguments)\n1231\t                               (u/lit []) raise)\n1232\t                        (outcome-node ok-tag (u/v result)))\n1233\t          refused (outcome-node\n1234\t                    error-tag\n1235\t                    (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n1236\t                           (u/lit :yang.call/not-callable)\n1237\t                           (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1238\t                                  (u/lit :yang.call/callee) (u/v callee))))\n1239\t          activation (u/if-node\n1240\t                       (u/app (u/v 'data/callable?) (u/v escape))\n1241\t                       common-call\n1242\t                       ;; Applying the escape resumes the capture operand.\n1243\t                       ;; Only our authenticated transfer packet may resume\n1244\t                       ;; here; an invalid captured value explicitly refuses.\n1245\t                       (u/if-node\n1246\t                         (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1247\t                                (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v escape)\n1248\t                                       (u/lit :clj/escape-token))\n1249\t                                (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1250\t                         (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v escape) (u/lit :clj/outcome))\n1251\t                         (outcome-node\n1252\t                           error-tag\n1253\t                           (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n1254\t                                  (u/lit :yang.call/invalid-invocation)\n1255\t                                  (u/lit {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit})))))\n1256\t          public-bridge (u/app (u/lam [escape] activation) u/capture)\n1257\t          bridged (if tail?\n1258\t                    (u/if-node\n1259\t                      (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v callee) (u/lit :clj/outcomes?))\n1260\t                      (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/invoke-with)\n1261\t                             (u/v callee) (u/v arguments) (u/lit [])\n1262\t                             (u/lam [condition] condition->outcome)\n1263\t                             (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1264\t                                    (u/lit :clj/outcome-token) (u/v 'dsg__call_token)))\n1265\t                      public-bridge)\n1266\t                    public-bridge)\n1267\t          admitted (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__admitted?) (u/v callee))\n1268\t                              bridged refused)\n1269\t          ;; A callee carrying a call entry is convention territory whether it\n1270\t          ;; admits or forges one, so admission rules it. Everything else is a\n1271\t          ;; data-side invocation - a collection lookup or a raw closure call -\n1272\t          ;; and the guest library's invoker owns those semantics. The invoker\n1273\t          ;; is itself a published descriptor, so it is reached the same way\n1274\t          ;; any guest callee is; its raise escapes to a capture of this site\n1275\t          ;; and the resumed pass materializes the error outcome here.\n1276\t          value-call (u/app\n1277\t                       (u/lam ['dsg__raise_escape]\n1278\t                              (u/if-node\n1279\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/callable?) (u/v 'dsg__raise_escape))\n1280\t                                (u/let1\n1281\t                                  (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invoker_result\"))\n1282\t                                  (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/invoke)\n1283\t                                         (u/v 'invoke-value)\n1284\t                                         (u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) (u/v callee) (u/v arguments))\n1285\t                                         (u/lit [])\n1286\t                                         (u/lam [condition]\n1287\t                                                (assoc (u/app (u/v 'dsg__raise_escape)\n1288\t                                                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1289\t                                                                     (u/lit :clj/escape-token) (u/v 'dsg__call_token)\n1290\t                                                                     (u/lit :clj/outcome) condition->outcome))\n1291\t                                                       :tail? true)))\n1292\t                                  (outcome-node ok-tag (u/v (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"invoker_result\")))))\n1293\t                                (u/if-node\n1294\t                                  (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1295\t                                         (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__raise_escape)\n1296\t                                                (u/lit :clj/escape-token))\n1297\t                                         (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1298\t                                  (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__raise_escape) (u/lit :clj/outcome))\n1299\t                                  (outcome-node\n1300\t                                    error-tag\n1301\t                                    (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n1302\t                                           (u/lit :yang.call/invalid-invocation)\n1303\t                                           (u/lit {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}))))))\n1304\t                       u/capture)\n1305\t          routed (if (::invoker env)\n1306\t                   (u/if-node\n1307\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/map?) (u/v callee))\n1308\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) (u/v callee) (u/lit :yang.call/entry))\n1309\t                                (u/lit false))\n1310\t                     admitted\n1311\t                     value-call)\n1312\t                   admitted)]\n1313\t      (cond-> (u/mark-tails (u/let1 callee callee-ast\n1314\t                                    (u/let1 arguments arguments-ast routed)))\n1315\t        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n1316\t\n1317\t\n1318\t(defn- compile-apply\n1319\t  \"(apply f a b coll) as one application of f to the assembled argument\n1320\t   vector (into [a b] (vec coll)): the convention's own calling shape, so it\n1321\t   serves a guest closure and an adapted native alike.\"\n1322\t  [operands env tail? macro-env]\n1323\t  (when (< (count operands) 2)\n1324\t    (reject! \"apply takes a function and an argument collection\"\n1325\t             {:operands (count operands)}))\n1326\t  (let [[f & more] operands\n1327\t        lead (vec (butlast more))\n1328\t        coll-form (list 'vec (last more))]\n1329\t    (compile-guest-call (compile-form f false env macro-env)\n1330\t                        (compile-form (if (seq lead)\n1331\t                                        (list 'data/into lead coll-form)\n1332\t                                        coll-form)\n1333\t                                      false env macro-env)\n1334\t                        env tail?)))\n1335\t\n1336\t\n1337\t(defn- compile-av-application\n1338\t  [operator operands env tail? macro-env]\n1339\t  (cond\n1340\t    (apply-call? env operator) (compile-apply operands env tail? macro-env)\n1341\t\n1342\t    ;; (:k m) / (:k m default): a static lookup\n1343\t    (keyword? operator)\n1344\t    (do (when-not (<= 1 (count operands) 2)\n1345\t          (reject! \"A keyword call takes a map and an optional default\"\n1346\t                   {:keyword operator, :operands (count operands)}))\n1347\t        (when (contains? (locals env) 'get)\n1348\t          (reject! \"A local binding of get would capture a keyword lookup\"\n1349\t                   {:keyword operator}))\n1350\t        (cond-> {:type :application\n1351\t                 :operator {:type :variable, :name 'get}\n1352\t                 :operands (into [(compile-form (first operands) false env macro-env)\n1353\t                                  (compile-literal operator false)]\n1354\t                                 (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env))\n1355\t                                 (rest operands))}\n1356\t          tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n1357\t\n1358\t    (and (outcomes? env) (= operator 'yang.call/eligible?))\n1359\t    (let [candidate 'dsg__eligibility_candidate]\n1360\t      (cond-> (u/mark-tails\n1361\t                (apply u/app\n1362\t                       (u/lam [candidate]\n1363\t                              (u/if-node\n1364\t                                (u/app (u/v 'dsg__admitted?) (u/v candidate))\n1365\t                                (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/eligible?) (u/v candidate))\n1366\t                                (u/lit false)))\n1367\t                       (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)))\n1368\t        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n1369\t\n1370\t    (and (outcomes? env)\n1371\t         (#{'yang.call/invoke 'yang.call/invoke-with} operator)\n1372\t         (<= 4 (count operands)))\n1373\t    (let [bindings (into ['dsg__invocation_candidate]\n1374\t                         (map #(symbol (str \"dsg__invocation_operand_\" %)))\n1375\t                         (range (dec (count operands))))\n1376\t          compile-operand #(compile-form % false env macro-env)]\n1377\t      (cond-> (u/mark-tails\n1378\t                (apply u/app\n1379\t                       (u/lam bindings\n1380\t                              (u/if-node\n1381\t                                (u/app (u/v 'dsg__admitted?) (u/v (first bindings)))\n1382\t                                (apply u/app (u/v operator) (map u/v bindings))\n1383\t                                (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/transfer)\n1384\t                                       (u/v (nth bindings 3))\n1385\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/condition)\n1386\t                                              (u/lit :yang.call/not-callable)\n1387\t                                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1388\t                                                     (u/lit :yang.call/callee)\n1389\t                                                     (u/v (first bindings)))))))\n1390\t                       (map compile-operand operands)))\n1391\t        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n1392\t\n1393\t    ;; a statically native name: call it directly\n1394\t    (native-name? env operator)\n1395\t    (cond-> {:type :application\n1396\t             :operator (cond-> {:type :variable, :name operator}\n1397\t                         (seq (meta operator)) (with-meta (meta operator)))\n1398\t             :operands (mapv #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)}\n1399\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\n1400\t\n1401\t    ;; anything else: one guest invocation, in tail position when the call is\n1402\t    :else\n1403\t    (compile-guest-call (compile-form operator false env macro-env)\n1404\t                        (compile-form (vec operands) false env macro-env)\n1405\t                        env tail?)))\n1406\t\n1407\t\n1408\t(defn compile-application\n1409\t  \"Compile a function application to Universal AST.\n1410\t\n1411\t  Clojure: (+ 1 2)\n1412\t  AST: {:type :application\n1413\t        :operator <compiled-operator>\n1414\t        :operands [<compiled-operand1> <compiled-operand2>]}\n1415\t\n1416\t  Under the argument-vector convention a user-function call passes its\n1417\t  operands as one vector.\"\n1418\t  ([operator operands env tail?] (compile-application operator operands env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1419\t  ([operator operands env tail? macro-env]\n1420\t   (if (and (::convention env) (not (macro-call? env macro-env operator)))\n1421\t     (compile-av-application operator operands env tail? macro-env)\n1422\t     (let [compiled-operator (compile-form operator false env macro-env)\n1423\t           compiled-operands (mapv #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)]\n1424\t       (cond-> {:type :application,\n1425\t                :operator compiled-operator,\n1426\t                :operands compiled-operands}\n1427\t         tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\n1428\t\n1429\t\n1430\t(defn compile-dao-stream-apply-call\n1431\t  \"Compile a dao.stream.apply call form to Universal AST.\n1432\t\n1433\t  Clojure: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\n1434\t  AST: {:type :dao.stream.apply/call\n1435\t        :op :op/name\n1436\t        :operands [<compiled-arg1> <compiled-arg2>]}\"\n1437\t  ([op operands env tail?] (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op operands env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1438\t  ([op operands env tail? macro-env]\n1439\t   (when-not (keyword? op)\n1440\t     (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.apply/call op must be a keyword\" {:op op})))\n1441\t   (let [compiled-operands (mapv #(compile-form % false env macro-env) operands)]\n1442\t     (cond-> {:type :dao.stream.apply/call,\n1443\t              :op op,\n1444\t              :operands compiled-operands}\n1445\t       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n1446\t\n1447\t\n1448\t(defn compile-if\n1449\t  \"Compile a conditional (if) expression to Universal AST.\n1450\t\n1451\t  Clojure: (if test consequent alternate)\n1452\t  AST: {:type :if\n1453\t        :test <compiled-test>\n1454\t        :consequent <compiled-consequent>\n1455\t        :alternate <compiled-alternate>}\n1456\t\n1457\t  An explicit `false` alternate is a value, not an absence: `alternate-present?`\n1458\t  distinguishes (if t c) from (if t c false).\"\n1459\t  ([test consequent alternate env tail?]\n1460\t   (compile-if test consequent alternate true env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1461\t  ([test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail?]\n1462\t   (compile-if test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1463\t  ([test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail? macro-env]\n1464\t   (cond-> {:type :if,\n1465\t            :test (compile-form test false env macro-env),\n1466\t            :consequent (compile-form consequent tail? env macro-env),\n1467\t            :alternate (if alt-present?\n1468\t                         (compile-form alternate tail? env macro-env)\n1469\t                         (compile-literal nil tail?))}\n1470\t     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n1471\t\n1472\t\n1473\t(declare compile-let-simple)\n1474\t\n1475\t\n1476\t(defn compile-let\n1477\t  \"Compile a let binding to Universal AST.\n1478\t\n1479\t  Transforms let into nested lambda applications:\n1480\t  (let [x 1 y 2] (+ x y))\n1481\t  =>\n1482\t  ((fn [x] ((fn [y] (+ x y)) 2)) 1)\"\n1483\t  ([bindings body env tail?] (compile-let bindings body env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1484\t  ([bindings body env tail? macro-env]\n1485\t   (compile-let-simple (expand-bindings bindings env) body env tail? macro-env)))\n1486\t\n1487\t\n1488\t(defn- compile-let-simple\n1489\t  \"compile-let over a binding vector whose targets are all plain symbols.\"\n1490\t  [bindings body env tail? macro-env]\n1491\t  (if (empty? bindings)\n1492\t    ;; a function body is compiled in the scope the bindings built\n1493\t    (if (fn? body)\n1494\t      (body tail? env macro-env)\n1495\t      (compile-form body tail? env macro-env))\n1496\t    (let [[binding-name binding-value & rest-bindings] bindings\n1497\t          compiled-value (compile-form binding-value false env macro-env)\n1498\t          new-macro-env (shadow-macro-env macro-env [binding-name])\n1499\t          compiled-body (compile-let-simple rest-bindings body\n1500\t                                            (with-locals env [binding-name])\n1501\t                                            tail? new-macro-env)]\n1502\t      (cond-> {:type :application,\n1503\t               :operator\n1504\t               {:type :lambda, :params [binding-name], :body compiled-body},\n1505\t               :operands [compiled-value]}\n1506\t        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n1507\t\n1508\t\n1509\t(defn compile-do\n1510\t  \"Compile a do block to Universal AST.\n1511\t\n1512\t  Transforms do into nested let expressions that evaluate and discard\n1513\t  intermediate results:\n1514\t  (do expr1 expr2 expr3)\n1515\t  =>\n1516\t  (let [_ expr1 _ expr2] expr3)\"\n1517\t  ([exprs env tail?] (compile-do exprs env tail? initial-macro-env))\n1518\t  ([exprs env tail? macro-env]\n1519\t   (if (empty? exprs)\n1520\t     (compile-literal nil tail?)\n1521\t     (if (= 1 (count exprs))\n1522\t       (compile-form (first exprs) tail? env macro-env)\n1523\t       (let [[first-expr & rest-exprs] exprs\n1524\t             compiled-first (compile-form first-expr false env macro-env)\n1525\t             compiled-rest (compile-do rest-exprs env tail? macro-env)]\n1526\t         (cond-> {:type :application,\n1527\t                  :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_], :body compiled-rest},\n1528\t                  :operands [compiled-first]}\n1529\t           tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))))\n1530\t\n1531\t\n1532\t;; =============================================================================\n1533\t;; loop/recur through lexical self-application (slice 4)\n1534\t;; =============================================================================\n1535\t;;\n1536\t;;   (loop [a i1 b i2] body)\n1537\t;;   =>  (let [a i1 b i2]                         ; sequential initializers\n1538\t;;         (let [dsg__loop0 (fn [dsg__loop0 a b] body')]\n1539\t;;           (dsg__loop0 dsg__loop0 a b)))\n1540\t;;\n1541\t;; where body' replaces each (recur x y) with the tail application\n1542\t;; (dsg__loop0 dsg__loop0 x y). The worker receives itself, so it needs no\n1543\t;; fixed-point combinator, definition or cell. It is compiler-internal and\n1544\t;; never first-class, so it keeps the native calling convention under the\n1545\t;; argument-vector convention too. A pattern binder becomes a fresh simple\n1546\t;; worker parameter and the worker body re-destructures it on each\n1547\t;; iteration. The recur target rides in the env: loop installs it, a source\n1548\t;; fn boundary resets it, let/do/if pass it on unchanged, and recur is legal\n1549\t;; only in tail position with the target's operand count.\n1550\t\n1551\t(defn- check-top-level!\n1552\t  \"Under the argument-vector convention the ::defined scan reads only\n1553\t   top-level heads, so a nested definition would dispatch against a name the\n1554\t   scan never saw.\"\n1555\t  [env top? operator]\n1556\t  (when (and (::convention env) (not top?))\n1557\t    (reject! (str operator \" is only supported at the top level under the argument-vector convention\")\n1558\t             {:operator operator})))\n1559\t\n1560\t\n1561\t(defn- compile-loop\n1562\t  [operands env tail? macro-env fn-loop?]\n1563\t  (let [[bindings & body-forms] operands]\n1564\t    (when-not (and (vector? bindings) (even? (count bindings)))\n1565\t      (reject! \"loop requires an even-sized binding vector\" {:bindings bindings}))\n1566\t    (let [outer (expand-bindings bindings env)\n1567\t          depth (::loop-depth env 0)\n1568\t          self (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"loop\" depth))\n1569\t          targets (map first (partition 2 bindings))\n1570\t          params (vec (map-indexed (fn [i t]\n1571\t                                     (if (vector? t)\n1572\t                                       (temp-symbol (str \"lp\" i) (meta t))\n1573\t                                       t))\n1574\t                                   targets))\n1575\t          args (vec (map-indexed (fn [i t]\n1576\t                                   (if (vector? t) (temp-symbol i (meta t)) t))\n1577\t                                 targets))\n1578\t          patterns (into [] (comp (map-indexed vector)\n1579\t                                  (filter (comp vector? second))\n1580\t                                  (mapcat (fn [[i t]] [t (params i)])))\n1581\t                         targets)\n1582\t          body-form (cond->> (body-expression body-forms)\n1583\t                      (seq patterns) (list 'let patterns))\n1584\t          worker-params (into [self] params)\n1585\t          build (fn [tail? env macro-env]\n1586\t                  (let [worker {:type :lambda\n1587\t                                :params worker-params\n1588\t                                :body (compile-form\n1589\t                                        body-form true\n1590\t                                        (with-locals\n1591\t                                          (assoc env\n1592\t                                                 ::target {:self self, :count (count params)\n1593\t                                                           :kind (if fn-loop?\n1594\t                                                                   \"fn parameters\"\n1595\t                                                                   \"loop bindings\")}\n1596\t                                                 ::loop-depth (inc depth))\n1597\t                                          worker-params)\n1598\t                                        (shadow-macro-env macro-env params))}]\n1599\t                    (cond-> {:type :application\n1600\t                             :operator {:type :lambda\n1601\t                                        :params [self]\n1602\t                                        :body (cond-> {:type :application\n1603\t                                                       :operator (compile-variable self false)\n1604\t                                                       :operands (into [(compile-variable self false)]\n1605\t                                                                       (map #(compile-variable % false))\n1606\t                                                                       args)}\n1607\t                                                tail? (assoc :tail? true))}\n1608\t                             :operands [worker]}\n1609\t                      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))]\n1610\t      (compile-let-simple outer build env tail? macro-env))))\n1611\t\n1612\t\n1613\t(defn- compile-recur\n1614\t  [operands env tail? macro-env]\n1615\t  (let [{:keys [self kind], n :count} (::target env)]\n1616\t    (when-not self\n1617\t      (reject! \"recur needs an enclosing loop or fn\" {:operands operands}))\n1618\t    (when-not (= n (count operands))\n1619\t      (reject! (str \"recur operand count differs from the \" kind)\n1620\t               {:expected n, :operands (count operands)}))\n1621\t    (when-not tail?\n1622\t      (reject! \"recur is only legal in tail position\" {:operands operands}))\n1623\t    {:type :application\n1624\t     :operator (compile-variable self false)\n1625\t     :operands (into [(compile-variable self false)]\n1626\t                     (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env))\n1627\t                     operands)\n1628\t     :tail? true}))\n1629\t\n1630\t\n1631\t;; =============================================================================\n1632\t;; case and the standard control forms as compile-time lowerings (slice 6)\n1633\t;; =============================================================================\n1634\t;;\n1635\t;; These are compiler forms, not runtime macros: each rewrites to if/let/do\n1636\t;; and compiles the result, so tail position and any later lowering of those\n1637\t;; primitives apply to them unchanged. Temporaries bind through the internal\n1638\t;; `dsg__let` (no binder check) under the reserved prefix; the name carries a\n1639\t;; nesting depth so an expansion inside an expansion never shadows its parent.\n1640\t;;\n1641\t;;   (case e k1 v1 (k2 k3) v2 default)\n1642\t;;   =>  (dsg__let [dsg__case0 e]\n1643\t;;         (if (= dsg__case0 'k1) v1\n1644\t;;           (if (if (= dsg__case0 'k2) true (= dsg__case0 'k3)) v2 default)))\n1645\t;;\n1646\t;; Constants are data (quoted), never evaluated. Without a default the\n1647\t;; fall-through applies the unbound `dsg__case-no-match` to the quoted form\n1648\t;; name and the scrutinee, so no match is a runtime failure, never nil.\n1649\t\n1650\t(defn- gen-name\n1651\t  [env tag]\n1652\t  (symbol (str reserved-prefix tag (::gen-depth env 0))))\n1653\t\n1654\t\n1655\t(defn- deeper\n1656\t  [env]\n1657\t  (update env ::gen-depth (fnil inc 0)))\n1658\t\n1659\t\n1660\t(defn- constant-test\n1661\t  [g constant]\n1662\t  (list '= g (if (or (symbol? constant) (seq? constant) (vector? constant)\n1663\t                     (map? constant) (set? constant))\n1664\t               (list 'quote constant)\n1665\t               constant)))\n1666\t\n1667\t\n1668\t(defn- clause-constants\n1669\t  \"The test constants of one case clause key: a list groups them, except a\n1670\t   quoted form (quote c), which is the one constant c.\"\n1671\t  [k]\n1672\t  (cond\n1673\t    (and (seq? k) (= 'quote (first k)) (= 2 (count k))) [(second k)]\n1674\t    (seq? k) (vec k)\n1675\t    :else [k]))\n1676\t\n1677\t\n1678\t(defn- case-clause-test\n1679\t  [g k]\n1680\t  (let [cs (clause-constants k)]\n1681\t    (if (= 1 (count cs))\n1682\t      (constant-test g (first cs))\n1683\t      (reduce (fn [else c] (list 'if (constant-test g c) true else))\n1684\t              false\n1685\t              (reverse cs)))))\n1686\t\n1687\t\n1688\t(defn- no-match-form\n1689\t  \"The fall-through of a case without a default: under the outcome model a\n1690\t   throw, which lowers to the error outcome naming the form.\"\n1691\t  [env g]\n1692\t  (if (outcomes? env)\n1693\t    (list 'throw {:yin.k/message \"No matching clause in case\"\n1694\t                  :yin.k/data {:yin.k/form (list 'quote 'case), :yin.k/value g}})\n1695\t    (list 'dsg__case-no-match ''case g)))\n1696\t\n1697\t\n1698\t(defn- expand-case\n1699\t  [env operands g]\n1700\t  (when (empty? operands)\n1701\t    (reject! \"case requires an expression\" {}))\n1702\t  (let [[e & clauses] operands\n1703\t        pairs (partition 2 clauses)\n1704\t        default? (odd? (count clauses))\n1705\t        constants (mapcat (fn [[k _]] (clause-constants k)) pairs)]\n1706\t    (when (empty? clauses)\n1707\t      (reject! \"case requires at least one clause\" {:form (cons 'case operands)}))\n1708\t    (when-not (apply distinct? (or (seq constants) [::none]))\n1709\t      (reject! \"case has duplicate test constants\"\n1710\t               {:duplicates (keys (remove (comp #{1} val) (frequencies constants)))}))\n1711\t    (list 'dsg__let [g e]\n1712\t          (reduce (fn [else [k v]] (list 'if (case-clause-test g k) v else))\n1713\t                  (if default?\n1714\t                    (last clauses)\n1715\t                    (no-match-form env g))\n1716\t                  (reverse pairs)))))\n1717\t\n1718\t\n1719\t(defn- expand-cond\n1720\t  [operands]\n1721\t  (when (odd? (count operands))\n1722\t    (reject! \"cond requires an even number of forms\" {:operands operands}))\n1723\t  (reduce (fn [else [t e]] (list 'if t e else))\n1724\t          nil\n1725\t          (reverse (partition 2 operands))))\n1726\t\n1727\t\n1728\t(defn- check-test-binding!\n1729\t  [operator bindings]\n1730\t  (when-not (and (vector? bindings) (= 2 (count bindings)))\n1731\t    (reject! (str operator \" requires a vector of one binding and a test\")\n1732\t             {:bindings bindings})))\n1733\t\n1734\t\n1735\t(defn- expand-if-let\n1736\t  [operator operands g]\n1737\t  (let [[bindings then else] operands]\n1738\t    (when-not (<= 2 (count operands) 3)\n1739\t      (reject! (str operator \" takes a binding vector, a then form and an optional else form\")\n1740\t               {:operands operands}))\n1741\t    (check-test-binding! operator bindings)\n1742\t    (let [[b t] bindings\n1743\t          bound (list 'let [b g] then)]\n1744\t      (list 'dsg__let [g t]\n1745\t            (if (= 'if-some operator)\n1746\t              (list 'if (list '= g nil) else bound)\n1747\t              (list 'if g bound else))))))\n1748\t\n1749\t\n1750\t(defn- expand-control\n1751\t  \"The if/let/do form a case or standard control form lowers to. A temporary\n1752\t   is named from the outcome pass's counter when one is running, else from the\n1753\t   nesting depth.\"\n1754\t  [env head operands]\n1755\t  (let [temp (fn [tag] (if (::gen env) (gen-sym env) (gen-name env tag)))]\n1756\t    (case head\n1757\t      case (expand-case env operands (temp \"case\"))\n1758\t      cond (expand-cond operands)\n1759\t      when (let [[test & body] operands]\n1760\t             (list 'if test (cons 'do body) nil))\n1761\t      if-let (expand-if-let head operands (temp \"iflet\"))\n1762\t      if-some (expand-if-let head operands (temp \"ifsome\"))\n1763\t      -> (reduce (fn [value step]\n1764\t                   (if (seq? step)\n1765\t                     (rebuild step (list* (first step) value (rest step)))\n1766\t                     (list step value)))\n1767\t                 (first operands) (rest operands))\n1768\t      when-let (let [[bindings & body] operands]\n1769\t                 (expand-control env 'if-let [bindings (cons 'do body) nil]))\n1770\t      when-some (let [[bindings & body] operands]\n1771\t                  (expand-control env 'if-some [bindings (cons 'do body) nil])))))\n1772\t\n1773\t\n1774\t(defn- compile-lowered\n1775\t  [form tail? env macro-env]\n1776\t  (compile-form form tail? (deeper env) macro-env))\n1777\t\n1778\t\n1779\t(defn compile-quote\n1780\t  \"Compile a quoted form to Universal AST.\n1781\t\n1782\t  Quoted forms become literals.\"\n1783\t  [form tail?]\n1784\t  (compile-literal form tail?))\n1785\t\n1786\t\n1787\t(defn resolve-primitive\n1788\t  \"Resolve primitive operations in the environment.\n1789\t\n1790\t  Primitives like +, -, *, /, =, <, > are built into the Yin VM\n1791\t  and are accessed as variables.\"\n1792\t  [sym]\n1793\t  (when (contains? #{'+ '- '* '/ '= '< '>} sym) sym))\n1794\t\n1795\t\n1796\t(defn- adapt-head\n1797\t  \"`call` with an adapted primitive's head replaced by its adapter, so\n1798\t   yin.k/outcome-of observes the adapter's outcome, as a tail call would.\"\n1799\t  [env call]\n1800\t  (let [head (first call)]\n1801\t    (if (and (symbol? head) (native-name? env head) (contains? (adapters env) head))\n1802\t      (rebuild call (cons (get (adapters env) head) (rest call)))\n1803\t      call)))\n1804\t\n1805\t\n1806\t(defn- compile-form*\n1807\t  \"Compile a Clojure form to Universal AST.\n1808\t\n1809\t  This is the main entry point that dispatches to specific compilers\n1810\t  based on the form type.\n1811\t\n1812\t  macro-env: compile-time map of defmacro names in scope. A macro call is an\n1813\t  ordinary application; macro-env only stops the native defn lowering.\"\n1814\t  [form tail? env macro-env top?]\n1815\t  (cond\n1816\t    ;; Literals: constants self-evaluate; collections with dynamic elements\n1817\t    ;; lower to constructor calls so their elements evaluate like Clojure\n1818\t    (literal? form)\n1819\t    (if (constant-form? form)\n1820\t      (compile-literal form tail?)\n1821\t      (compile-constructed-collection form tail? env macro-env))\n1822\t    ;; The empty list is self-evaluating data, not an application\n1823\t    (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) (compile-literal form tail?)\n1824\t    ;; Variables (symbols)\n1825\t    (symbol? form) (if (native-name? env form)\n1826\t                     (if (outcomes? env)\n1827\t                       (compile-call-descriptor (compile-adapter form env false macro-env) tail?)\n1828\t                       (compile-adapter form env tail? macro-env))\n1829\t                     (compile-variable form tail?))\n1830\t    ;; Special forms and function application\n1831\t    (seq? form)\n1832\t    (let [[operator & operands] form]\n1833\t      (cond\n1834\t        ;; dao.stream.apply call: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\n1835\t        (= operator 'dao.stream.apply/call)\n1836\t        (let [[op & args] operands]\n1837\t          (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op args env tail? macro-env))\n1838\t        ;; (yin.k/outcome-of (f x)): the call's outcome as a value, not unwrapped\n1839\t        (and (= operator 'yin.k/outcome-of) (outcomes? env))\n1840\t        (compile-form (adapt-head env (first operands)) tail? env macro-env)\n1841\t        ;; Native defn fallback: used only when no defmacro defn is in scope\n1842\t        ;; and the form actually matches defn syntax.\n1843\t        (and (contains? #{'defn 'defn-} operator)\n1844\t             (not (contains? macro-env operator)))\n1845\t        (do (check-top-level! env top? operator)\n1846\t            (compile-defn operator operands env tail? macro-env))\n1847\t\n1848\t        ;; Special forms\n1849\t        :else\n1850\t        (case operator\n1851\t          ;; Lambda: (fn [params] body)\n1852\t          fn (if (::convention env)\n1853\t               (compile-av-fn (fn-arities operands) env tail? macro-env nil (source-meta form))\n1854\t               (let [[params & body] operands]\n1855\t                 (compile-fn params body env tail? macro-env)))\n1856\t          ;; Conditional: (if test consequent alternate?)\n1857\t          if (let [[test consequent alternate] operands]\n1858\t               (compile-if test consequent alternate (> (count operands) 2) env tail? macro-env))\n1859\t          ;; Let binding: (let [bindings] body)\n1860\t          let (let [[bindings & body] operands\n1861\t                    body-expr (if (= 1 (count body)) (first body) (cons 'do body))]\n1862\t                (compile-let bindings body-expr env tail? macro-env))\n1863\t          ;; Do block: (do expr1 expr2 ...)\n1864\t          do (compile-do operands env tail? macro-env)\n1865\t          loop (compile-loop operands env tail? macro-env (::fn-loop (meta form)))\n1866\t          ;; (yin.k/outcome-of (f x)): the call's outcome as a value, not unwrapped\n1867\t          ;; internal, from the outcome lowering: its bindings are already plain\n1868\t          dsg__let (compile-let-simple (first operands) (body-expression (rest operands))\n1869\t                                       env tail? macro-env)\n1870\t          recur (compile-recur operands env tail? macro-env)\n1871\t          (case cond when if-let if-some when-let when-some ->)\n1872\t          (compile-lowered (expand-control env operator operands)\n1873\t                           tail? env macro-env)\n1874\t          ;; Short-circuit logical: expand to if chains so unevaluated operands are never touched\n1875\t          ;; (and)       → true\n1876\t          ;; (and x)     → x\n1877\t          ;; (and x y z) → (dsg__let [g x] (if g (and y z) g))\n1878\t          and (cond\n1879\t                (empty? operands) {:type :literal :value true}\n1880\t                (= 1 (count operands)) (compile-form (first operands) tail? env macro-env)\n1881\t                :else (let [g (gen-name env \"and\")]\n1882\t                        (compile-lowered (list 'dsg__let [g (first operands)]\n1883\t                                               (list 'if g (cons 'and (rest operands)) g))\n1884\t                                         tail? env macro-env)))\n1885\t          ;; (or)        → nil\n1886\t          ;; (or x)      → x\n1887\t          ;; (or x y z)  → (dsg__let [g x] (if g g (or y z)))\n1888\t          or  (cond\n1889\t                (empty? operands) {:type :literal :value nil}\n1890\t                (= 1 (count operands)) (compile-form (first operands) tail? env macro-env)\n1891\t                :else (let [g (gen-name env \"or\")]\n1892\t                        (compile-lowered (list 'dsg__let [g (first operands)]\n1893\t                                               (list 'if g g (cons 'or (rest operands))))\n1894\t                                         tail? env macro-env)))\n1895\t          ;; Quote: (quote form)\n1896\t          quote (compile-quote (first operands) tail?)\n1897\t          ;; Def: (def sym value)\n1898\t          def (let [[sym value] operands]\n1899\t                (check-top-level! env top? operator)\n1900\t                (compile-def sym value env tail? macro-env))\n1901\t          ;; Macro definition: (defmacro name params & body)\n1902\t          defmacro (do (check-top-level! env top? operator)\n1903\t                       (compile-defmacro operands env tail? macro-env))\n1904\t          ;; Function application: (f arg1 arg2 ...)\n1905\t          (compile-application operator operands env tail? macro-env))))\n1906\t    ;; Unknown form type\n1907\t    :else (throw (ex-info \"Cannot compile unknown form type\"\n1908\t                          {:form form,\n1909\t                           :type #?(:cljd (clojure.core/str (.-runtimeType form))\n1910\t                                    :default (clojure.core/type form))}))))\n1911\t\n1912\t\n1913\t(defn compile-form\n1914\t  \"Compile one Clojure form and retain the reader's plain metadata on the\n1915\t   emitted Universal AST node. The tuple boundary removes it from content\n1916\t   and writes positions and other frontend facts to occurrence side tables.\"\n1917\t  ([form] (compile-form form false {} initial-macro-env))\n1918\t  ([form env] (compile-form form false env initial-macro-env))\n1919\t  ([form tail? env] (compile-form form tail? env initial-macro-env))\n1920\t  ([form tail? env macro-env]\n1921\t   (let [ast (compile-form* form tail? (dissoc env ::top-level) macro-env\n1922\t                            (::top-level env))\n1923\t         m (meta form)]\n1924\t     (if (seq (dissoc m ::fn-loop))\n1925\t       (vary-meta ast merge (dissoc m ::fn-loop))\n1926\t       ast))))\n1927\t\n1928\t\n1929\t(defn- program-env\n1930\t  \"The compile-time env of one program. Without `opts` it is empty: the\n1931\t   native path. `{:convention :arg-vector, :native #{symbol}, :macros\n1932\t   #{symbol}}` opts into the argument-vector convention: `:native` names the\n1933\t   primitives a bare symbol may call directly (a set, or a map from name to\n1934\t   its published profile, whose `:yin.k/arities` give an adapter its admitted\n1935\t   counts), `:macros` the expander-side\n1936\t   macro names whose calls must stay ordinary applications. The program's\n1937\t   own top-level definitions are never native. `:outcomes true` adds the\n1938\t   outcome model (see its section); `:adapters` maps a primitive that\n1939\t   declares domain failures to the host adapter returning its outcome.\"\n1940\t  [forms opts]\n1941\t  (if-not opts\n1942\t    {}\n1943\t    (do (when-not (= :arg-vector (:convention opts))\n1944\t          (reject! \"Unknown compile-program convention\" {:opts opts}))\n1945\t        (when-let [hit (seq (filter control-heads (:macros opts)))]\n1946\t          (reject! \"A :macros entry names a compiler form\" {:macros (vec hit)}))\n1947\t        (let [defined (into #{}\n1948\t                            (keep (fn [f]\n1949\t                                    (when (and (seq? f)\n1950\t                                               (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first f))\n1951\t                                               (symbol? (second f)))\n1952\t                                      (strip-symbol-meta (second f)))))\n1953\t                            forms)]\n1954\t          ;; the compiler emits bare conj and vec (collection literals, apply),\n1955\t          ;; so a program definition of either would capture them\n1956\t          (when-let [hit (first (filter #{'conj 'vec} defined))]\n1957\t            (reject! (str \"Defining \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n1958\t                     {:name hit}))\n1959\t          (cond-> {::convention {:native (set (if (map? (:native opts))\n1960\t                                                (keys (:native opts))\n1961\t                                                (:native opts)))\n1962\t                                 :arities (into {}\n1963\t                                                (keep (fn [[sym profile]]\n1964\t                                                        (when-let [a (if (map? profile)\n1965\t                                                                       (:yin.k/arities profile)\n1966\t                                                                       profile)]\n1967\t                                                          [sym a])))\n1968\t                                                (when (map? (:native opts)) (:native opts)))\n1969\t                                 :macros (set (:macros opts))}\n1970\t                   ::defined defined\n1971\t                   ::invoker (boolean (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defn (first %))\n1972\t                                                  (= 'invoke-value (second %))\n1973\t                                                  (:yin.k/invoker (meta (second %)))) forms))}\n1974\t            (:outcomes opts) (assoc ::outcomes {:adapters (or (:adapters opts) {})}))))))\n1975\t\n1976\t\n1977\t(defn- check-program-symbols!\n1978\t  \"The program pre-pass. Quoted data is exempt. The reserved prefix names\n1979\t   compiler temporaries, so no user symbol may carry it in ANY position\n1980\t   (binder, reference, definition name); `loop` and `recur` are special forms,\n1981\t   so they may only head a list, never stand as a value or a binder.\"\n1982\t  [form]\n1983\t  (cond\n1984\t    (symbol? form)\n1985\t    (do (when (reserved-name? form)\n1986\t          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n1987\t                   {:symbol form, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n1988\t        (when (and (nil? (namespace form)) (contains? #{'loop 'recur} form))\n1989\t          (reject! (str form \" is only legal in operator position\") {:symbol form})))\n1990\t    (seq? form)\n1991\t    (when-not (= 'quote (first form))\n1992\t      (let [head (first form)]\n1993\t        (when (and (symbol? head) (reserved-name? head))\n1994\t          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n1995\t                   {:symbol head, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n1996\t        (when-not (symbol? head)\n1997\t          (check-program-symbols! head))\n1998\t        (run! check-program-symbols! (rest form))))\n1999\t    (map? form) (run! check-program-symbols! (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n2000\t    (coll? form) (run! check-program-symbols! form)))\n2001\t\n2002\t\n2003\t(defn- check-top-level-discard!\n2004\t  \"Only the last top-level form's outcome reaches the harness, so a non-final,\n2005\t   non-definition form that may fail would have its error silently discarded:\n2006\t   refuse it, as a def value that calls guest functions is refused. Returns\n2007\t   `form`.\"\n2008\t  [env macro-env forms form]\n2009\t  (when (and (next forms)\n2010\t             (not (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form))))\n2011\t             (failing? (assoc env ::macro-env macro-env) (rewrite-ex-info form)))\n2012\t    (reject! \"A non-final top-level form that may fail would discard its error outcome\"\n2013\t             {:form form}))\n2014\t  form)\n2015\t\n2016\t\n2017\t(defn- lower-top-form\n2018\t  \"Under the outcome model a top-level expression returns an outcome like a\n2019\t   function body; definitions keep their own lowering.\"\n2020\t  [env macro-env form]\n2021\t  (if (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form)))\n2022\t    form\n2023\t    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n2024\t\n2025\t\n2026\t(defn compile-program\n2027\t  \"Compile a sequence of Clojure forms into a single Universal AST.\n2028\t   Top-level defs compile to explicit yin/def store writes, sequenced via lambda.\n2029\t   Top-level defmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n2030\t   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n2031\t   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n2032\t   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n2033\t   convention (see `program-env`); without it the output is the native one.\"\n2034\t  ([forms] (compile-program forms true))\n2035\t  ([forms tail?] (compile-program forms tail? nil))\n2036\t  ([forms tail? opts]\n2037\t   (run! check-program-symbols! forms)\n2038\t   (let [env (program-env forms opts)]\n2039\t     ;; A discarded definition must not become a lexical binding in the\n2040\t     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n2041\t     ;; their environment: retaining the previous descriptor here doubles its\n2042\t     ;; paths at each definition during machine-data validation and UCF lift.\n2043\t     (letfn [(discard-result\n2044\t               [ast]\n2045\t               (if (outcomes? env) (u/then ast (u/lit nil)) ast))\n2046\t             (go\n2047\t               [forms macro-env]\n2048\t               (if (empty? forms)\n2049\t                 (compile-literal nil tail?)\n2050\t                 (let [head       (cond->> (first forms)\n2051\t                                    (outcomes? env) (check-top-level-discard! env macro-env forms)\n2052\t                                    (outcomes? env) (lower-top-form env macro-env))\n2053\t                       rest-forms (rest forms)]\n2054\t                   (cond\n2055\t                     ;; defmacro: ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax whose\n2056\t                     ;; lambda the encoder declares; later forms see the name\n2057\t                     ;; only so the native defn lowering can yield to it.\n2058\t                     (and (seq? head) (= 'defmacro (first head)))\n2059\t                     (let [defined (compile-defmacro (rest head) env false macro-env)]\n2060\t                       (cond-> {:type     :application\n2061\t                                :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ReiV2MboN4Oo9Zus8IjkGSq6","content":"1\t(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.python.antlr.prelude/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n2\t yang.python.antlr.prelude\n3\t  \"The Python runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n4\t   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.1, §8.2, §9.3). Python semantics for\n5\t   operators, truthiness, equality, objects, exceptions and escapes live\n6\t   here as guest code, not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications\n7\t   of these names.\n8\t\n9\t   Value encoding:\n10\t     int             host integer (untagged)\n11\t     float           {:py/float x}: tagged on every host, because JS cannot\n12\t                     tell 2 from 2.0 (owner decision 3); x is float64\n13\t                     content (`data/float64`), never a bare host number,\n14\t                     so 2.0 has one address on every host. Arithmetic\n15\t                     unwraps with `data/float-value` and computes on bare\n16\t                     host numbers. The prelude holds no integral float\n17\t                     literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1), and no float literal\n18\t                     reaches host arithmetic except through\n19\t                     `data/float-value`, which also bridges a float64\n20\t                     carrier decoded from a row back to a host number:\n21\t                     1.0 is written (data/float-value 1)\n22\t     bool            host true / false (numeric as 1 / 0)\n23\t     None            :py/None\n24\t     str             {:py/str \\\"...\\\"}\n25\t     list            a cell holding {:py/type :list :items [...]}\n26\t     dict            a cell holding {:py/type :dict :index {nkey slot}\n27\t                     :keys [...] :vals [...]}: insertion order is the keys\n28\t                     vector, never a host map's order; keys are normalized\n29\t                     so 1, 1.0 and True are one key (see `py/key`)\n30\t     set             a cell holding {:py/type :set :index {nkey slot}\n31\t                     :keys [...]}: insertion order, keys normalized as for\n32\t                     dicts\n33\t     function        a cell holding {:py/type :function :name s :spec spec\n34\t                     :defaults [...] :kwdefaults [[name v] ...]\n35\t                     :code (fn [args] ...) :yang.call/entry\n36\t                     (fn [invocation] ...)}; identity is the cell ref\n37\t     class           a cell holding {:py/type :class :name s :base cls\n38\t                     :attrs {name value}}\n39\t     instance        a cell holding {:py/type :instance :class cls\n40\t                     :attrs {name value}}\n41\t     generator       a cell holding {:py/type :generator :name s :state st}\n42\t                     and the slots of its state (see `py/gen-switch`)\n43\t     iterator        a cell holding {:py/type :iterator :src s :i n}: what\n44\t                     iter() makes of a sequence, advancing `py/iter-at` over\n45\t                     src once per next; src None once exhausted\n46\t     bound method    {:py/type :method :self obj :fn function}\n47\t     tuple           {:py/type :tuple :items [...]}: a value; hashable when\n48\t                     its elements are\n49\t     slice           {:py/type :slice :start a :stop b :step c}\n50\t     range           {:py/type :range :start a :stop b :step s}\n51\t     module globals  a dict (owner decision 1): the module body receives it\n52\t                     as `%globals` and every function closes over it, which\n53\t                     is Python's own `__globals__`; a miss falls back to the\n54\t                     builtins dict, and a miss there is NameError\n55\t     module          a cell {:py/type :module :name s :dict d :body f}: the\n56\t                     object `py/import` binds, its dict the module's own\n57\t                     namespace, so attribute reads, writes and deletes are\n58\t                     dict operations every function of the module sees, and\n59\t                     `__dict__` reads the cell's dict; sys.modules itself is\n60\t                     the dict `py.rt/modules`, `sys`, `builtins` and `importlib` the\n61\t                     module objects `py/init!` pre-seeds into it; :body\n62\t                     retains an imported module's image for reload\n63\t\n64\t   Calling convention: `py/call-kw` resolves Python methods and classes,\n65\t   then discovers admitted entries through `yang.call`. Python function\n66\t   entries bind positional arguments, keywords, defaults, `*args` and\n67\t   `**kwargs` before applying their private `:code`; entryless builtins keep\n68\t   their existing Python-local path.\n69\t\n70\t   Runtime state is allocated by `py/init!`, once per task, under the slot\n71\t   `py.rt/state` (the literal `:py/uninit` until `py/init!` flips it to\n72\t   `:py/ready` as its last write; a second call allocates nothing): the\n73\t   four cells below, the builtin classes and functions as `py.b/*` keys,\n74\t   and the builtins namespace dict `py.b/builtins`, which `py/global-get`\n75\t   falls back to. All of it is reached through the store (`yin/def`\n76\t   appears only in the prelude):\n77\t     py.rt/ctx       the dynamic context, one record\n78\t                     {:handlers :depth :base :frame}:\n79\t                     :handlers  the handler stack: frames\n80\t                                [kind payload rest n depth]; a :handler\n81\t                                frame holds the continuation `raise`\n82\t                                delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk every\n83\t                                exit through it runs (raise passes the\n84\t                                exception, escapes and normal completion\n85\t                                pass None), a :generator frame the bottom\n86\t                                of a running generator's own stack (raise\n87\t                                passes it the exception); nil when empty\n88\t                     :depth     the call depth within the current\n89\t                                activation: the safepoint hook prelude\n90\t                                counts it (RecursionError); the base\n91\t                                prelude only saves and restores it\n92\t                     :base      the absolute depth the activation runs\n93\t                                on: 0 outside generators; every crossing\n94\t                                into a generator sets it to the\n95\t                                resumer's absolute depth plus one (the\n96\t                                generator's own frame), so depth always\n97\t                                measures the current continuation\n98\t                     :frame     the current frame; nil, reserved for\n99\t                                tracing\n100\t     py.rt/limit     the recursion limit, 1000 by default; outside the\n101\t                     escape-restored record, so a change persists. A\n102\t                     generator start or resume is admitted only while its\n103\t                     frame fits; the hook prelude checks function entry\n104\t                     against it and sets it\n105\t     py.rt/out       the values `print` collected, one vector per call\n106\t     py.rt/value     the REPL submission's result: the snapshot of the last\n107\t                     bare expression statement it ran (None when none ran)\n108\t     py.rt/modules   sys.modules (C4 I1): the dict of py str name to module\n109\t                     object; an import consults it before anything else, a\n110\t                     miss is instantiated and inserted before its body\n111\t                     runs, and a raising body removes its entry again.\n112\t                     py.rt/sys and py.rt/builtins-mod are the two module\n113\t                     objects `py/init!` pre-seeds into it: `sys`, whose\n114\t                     dict holds py.rt/modules under the name modules, and\n115\t                     `builtins`, whose dict is the builtins namespace\n116\t\n117\t   Escapes and handlers tell the first pass through a capture point from a\n118\t   re-entry with a flag cell allocated before the capture (`:first`, then\n119\t   `:re-entered`): heap writes survive continuation invocation, so the flag\n120\t   answers without inspecting the continuation's representation. An escape\n121\t   unwinds the handler stack to the frame it captured, running finally\n122\t   thunks on the way, and restores the dynamic context saved at capture\n123\t   with the current `:base` left alone: an exception may unwind many\n124\t   calls, so the call depth is restored, never decremented, and it is\n125\t   restored relative to the activation it runs in. Only crossings rebase.\n126\t\n127\t   Integer arithmetic, bitwise operators and shifts are exact through\n128\t   the integer module, subject to the composition's resource limits.\n129\t   Float floor uses binary descent within its supported float range.\n130\t\n131\t   Numeric dict and set keys and `hash()` are exact (C3 rulings 6 and 7):\n132\t   a finite number keys as its reduced rational in lowercase hex text,\n133\t   to which no digit limit applies, and hashes modulo P = 2^61 - 1 on\n134\t   every host, both computed through the `integer` module's kernels. A\n135\t   float key or hash can need integers of 1075 bits (2^-1074), so the\n136\t   composition's `integer` limits must admit at least that.\n137\t\n138\t   The `integer` module (version 4) answers a limit breach as a reason,\n139\t   not a result, and `py/int-result` wraps every call that can breach:\n140\t   `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit` raises MemoryError, as CPython 3.9.6 does\n141\t   when an integer cannot be allocated, and `:yin.vm.integer/digit-limit`\n142\t   raises ValueError. CPython 3.9.6 has no digit limit (it arrived in\n143\t   3.9.14 and 3.11), so the digit limit is this support profile's\n144\t   restriction, not a 3.9.6 match; its message names the composition's\n145\t   limit, read through `integer/max-digits`. Float overflow raises\n146\t   OverflowError with \\\"int too large to convert to float\\\". The guest\n147\t   message is the prelude's, never host text. Every other refusal stays\n148\t   a host failure of the run: the prelude checks its causes before the\n149\t   call, so reaching one is a prelude defect, not a guest error.\n150\t\n151\t   The conversion builtins (C3 slice S4: int, float, str, repr, bool,\n152\t   abs, pow, hex, oct, bin, round) validate text here and leave digits\n153\t   to the kernels: `integer/parse`, `integer/decimal->float` (one\n154\t   rounding, no digit limit) and `integer/float-digits`, whose shortest\n155\t   digits `py/float-repr` lays out by the same rule as the boundary\n156\t   renderer. `print` checks the digit limit of every integer it shows\n157\t   before it appends anything.\n158\t\n159\t   Sequence repetition (C3 slice S7, ruling 11) checks the exact size of\n160\t   its result against the composition's `data/max-items` before it\n161\t   builds anything; a larger one raises MemoryError. A composition\n162\t   proves it supplies every host name, `data/max-items` and the version\n163\t   4 `integer` exports included, through `admit` before a program runs.\n164\t\n165\t   Two emitters, one source (C4 slice P2): `definitions` is the only\n166\t   definition list. `uast` is the bundled prelude a program tree carries\n167\t   ahead of its body; `module-uast` is the same list as the linker\n168\t   module `py` (`module-exports`, `module-spec`), which a linked program\n169\t   requires instead. The module emitter strips only the module's own\n170\t   namespace `py/`; `py.b/*` and `py.rt/*` stay qualified internal keys,\n171\t   each runtime key with a module-level `:py/uninit` placeholder so the\n172\t   linker's scanners discharge the bodies that read it before `py/init!`\n173\t   defines it. `py/vconj` and `py/lnot` are not `py/conj` and `py/not`\n174\t   because a bare key equal to a primitive name would shadow that\n175\t   primitive inside the module. `py/rt-ctx` and `py/rt-limit` (P3) hand\n176\t   the hook prelude the two cells this prelude owns, which a linked\n177\t   `pysp` closure cannot name across the module boundary.\n178\t\n179\t   Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`\n180\t   (the cell module from yin.vm.module, the integer module from\n181\t   yin.vm.integer, the rest from yin.vm.data).\"\n182\t  #?(:cljs (:require-macros [yang.python.antlr.prelude :refer [defquoted]]))\n183\t  (:require\n184\t    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n185\t    [yang.core.call :as call]\n186\t    [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n187\t    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\n188\t    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n189\t\n190\t\n191\t#?(:clj\n192\t   (defmacro defquoted\n193\t     \"`def` of the quoted data `form`.  ClojureDart compiles quoted data to\n194\t      straight-line Dart (this prelude is about 65,000 lines of it), which the\n195\t      Dart AOT compiler cannot take as one initializer, so there the data is\n196\t      one EDN string read back at load.\"\n197\t     [name doc form]\n198\t     (if (find-ns 'cljd.compiler)\n199\t       (list 'def name doc (list 'edn/read-string (pr-str (second form))))\n200\t       (list 'def name doc form))))\n201\t\n202\t\n203\t(def host-names\n204\t  \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n205\t  (into '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/into data/subvec\n206\t           data/number? data/contains? data/dissoc data/str-concat data/str-length\n207\t           data/str-index-of data/str->code-points data/code-points->str\n208\t           data/float64 data/float-value data/content=\n209\t           integer/add integer/sub integer/neg integer/mul integer/compare\n210\t           integer/to-float integer/compare-float integer/true-div\n211\t           integer/pow integer/shift-right integer/bit-and\n212\t           integer/bit-or integer/bit-xor integer/bit-not integer/from-float\n213\t           integer/floor-div-mod integer/shift-left integer/format integer/parse\n214\t           integer/float-digits integer/decimal->float integer/max-digits\n215\t           data/substring data/max-items}\n216\t        call/host-names))\n217\t\n218\t\n219\t(defquoted ^:private core-definitions\n220\t  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n221\t  '[;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- kinds\n222\t    [py/cell? (fn [x] (= (get x :type) :cell-ref))]\n223\t    [py/str? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/str))))]\n224\t    [py/str (fn [s] (assoc {} :py/str s))]\n225\t    [py/float? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/float))))]\n226\t    [py/float (fn [x] (assoc {} :py/float (data/float64 x)))]\n227\t    [py/tuple (fn [items] (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :tuple) :items items))]\n228\t    [py/vconj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n229\t    [py/arg (fn [args i] (get args i))]\n230\t    [py/numeric?\n231\t     (fn [x]\n232\t       (if (= x true)\n233\t         true\n234\t         (if (= x false) true (if (py/float? x) true (data/number? x)))))]\n235\t    [py/num\n236\t     (fn [x]\n237\t       (if (= x true)\n238\t         1\n239\t         (if (= x false)\n240\t           0\n241\t           (if (py/float? x) (data/float-value (get x :py/float)) x))))]\n242\t    [py/zero?\n243\t     (fn [x]\n244\t       (let [v (py/num x)] (if (= v 0) true (= v (data/float-value 0)))))]\n245\t    [py/content-type (fn [x] (if (py/cell? x) (get (cell/get x) :py/type) nil))]\n246\t    [py/function? (fn [x] (= (py/content-type x) :function))]\n247\t\n248\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n249\t    ;; The dynamic context is one record in one cell, {:handlers :depth\n250\t    ;; :base :frame}: every capture point saves it and every escape\n251\t    ;; restores it with the current :base left alone (`py/restore!`), so\n252\t    ;; an escape inside a generator restores its depth relative to the\n253\t    ;; activation it runs in; only crossings set :base. The handler stack\n254\t    ;; is a chain of frames [kind payload rest n depth]: :handler frames\n255\t    ;; hold the continuation `raise` delivers to, :finally frames hold a\n256\t    ;; thunk of one argument (the exception, or None) that every exit\n257\t    ;; through them runs. n, the frame count, makes \"unwind to here\" an\n258\t    ;; integer comparison; depth is the (activation-relative) call depth\n259\t    ;; the frame was pushed at, which its thunk runs at.\n260\t    [py/ctx\n261\t     (fn [handlers depth base frame]\n262\t       (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :handlers handlers) :depth depth)\n263\t                     :base base)\n264\t              :frame frame))]\n265\t    [py/abs-depth (fn [c] (+ (get c :base) (get c :depth)))]\n266\t    [py/rt-ctx\n267\t     ;; the dynamic-context cell itself (C4 slice P3): the base prelude\n268\t     ;; owns the record, and the hook prelude counts frames in it, but\n269\t     ;; `py.rt/*` is an internal store key no closure of another module\n270\t     ;; can name, so linked hooks read the cell through this export\n271\t     (fn [] py.rt/ctx)]\n272\t    [py/rt-limit\n273\t     ;; the recursion-limit cell, the same door\n274\t     (fn [] py.rt/limit)]\n275\t    [py/restore!\n276\t     (fn [saved]\n277\t       (cell/set! py.rt/ctx\n278\t                  (assoc saved :base (get (cell/get py.rt/ctx) :base))))]\n279\t    [py/handlers (fn [] (get (cell/get py.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\n280\t    [py/set-handlers!\n281\t     (fn [hs] (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (assoc (cell/get py.rt/ctx) :handlers hs)))]\n282\t    [py/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (nil? hs) 0 (get hs 3)))]\n283\t    [py/frame\n284\t     (fn [kind payload rest]\n285\t       (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] kind) payload) rest)\n286\t                           (+ 1 (py/frame-depth rest)))\n287\t                 (get (cell/get py.rt/ctx) :depth)))]\n288\t    [py/pop-frame\n289\t     ;; the handler stack below frame hs, at the call depth hs was pushed at\n290\t     (fn [hs]\n291\t       (cell/set! py.rt/ctx\n292\t                  (assoc (assoc (cell/get py.rt/ctx) :handlers (get hs 2))\n293\t                         :depth (get hs 4))))]\n294\t    [py/raise\n295\t     (fn [e]\n296\t       (let [hs (py/handlers)]\n297\t         (if (nil? hs)\n298\t           (:py/no-handler e)\n299\t           (if (= (get hs 0) :finally)\n300\t             (do (py/pop-frame hs)\n301\t                 ((get hs 1) e)\n302\t                 (py/raise e))\n303\t             ((get hs 1) e)))))]\n304\t    [py/unwind-to\n305\t     ;; pop frames above frame count n, running each finally thunk with None\n306\t     (fn [n]\n307\t       (let [hs (py/handlers)]\n308\t         (if (nil? hs)\n309\t           :py/None\n310\t           (if (<= (get hs 3) n)\n311\t             :py/None\n312\t             (do (py/pop-frame hs)\n313\t                 (if (= (get hs 0) :finally) ((get hs 1) :py/None) :py/None)\n314\t                 (py/unwind-to n))))))]\n315\t    [py/try\n316\t     (fn [body handler orelse]\n317\t       (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/ctx)\n318\t             flag (cell/new :first)]\n319\t         ((fn [r]\n320\t            (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n321\t              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n322\t                  (py/set-handlers! (py/frame :handler r (get saved :handlers)))\n323\t                  (body)\n324\t                  (py/restore! saved)\n325\t                  (orelse))\n326\t              (do (py/restore! saved)\n327\t                  (handler r))))\n328\t          (%capture))))]\n329\t    [py/try-finally\n330\t     ;; normal exit runs `fin` here; raise and escapes run it as they\n331\t     ;; unwind through the :finally frame\n332\t     (fn [body fin]\n333\t       (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/ctx)]\n334\t         (do (py/set-handlers! (py/frame :finally fin (get saved :handlers)))\n335\t             (let [v (body)]\n336\t               (do (py/restore! saved)\n337\t                   (fin :py/None)\n338\t                   v)))))]\n339\t    [py/call-ec\n340\t     (fn [f]\n341\t       (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/ctx)\n342\t             flag (cell/new :first)]\n343\t         ((fn [r]\n344\t            (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n345\t              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n346\t                  (f (fn [x]\n347\t                       (do (py/unwind-to (py/frame-depth (get saved :handlers)))\n348\t                           (py/restore! saved)\n349\t                           (r x)))))\n350\t              r))\n351\t          (%capture))))]\n352\t    [py/type-of\n353\t     (fn [x] (if (= (py/content-type x) :instance) (get (cell/get x) :class) :py/None))]\n354\t    [py/with\n355\t     ;; the language reference's expansion: __exit__ is looked up before\n356\t     ;; __enter__ runs; an exception calls __exit__(type, value, None) and\n357\t     ;; is suppressed when that is truthy; every other exit calls\n358\t     ;; __exit__(None, None, None)\n359\t     ;; Both dunders are looked up on the manager's type, as implicit\n360\t     ;; invocations are; an instance attribute of that name is not used.\n361\t     (fn [mgr suite]\n362\t       (let [cls (py/type-of mgr)\n363\t             enter-fn (if (= cls :py/None) :py/missing (py/class-lookup cls \"__enter__\"))\n364\t             exit-fn (if (= cls :py/None) :py/missing (py/class-lookup cls \"__exit__\"))]\n365\t         (if (if (= enter-fn :py/missing) true (= exit-fn :py/missing))\n366\t           (py/type-error\n367\t             {:py/str \"object does not support the context manager protocol\"})\n368\t           (py/with-bound mgr (py/bind mgr enter-fn) (py/bind mgr exit-fn) suite))))]\n369\t    [py/with-bound\n370\t     (fn [mgr enter exit suite]\n371\t       (let [value (py/call enter [])\n372\t             hit (cell/new false)]\n373\t         (py/try-finally\n374\t           (fn []\n375\t             (py/try (fn [] (suite value))\n376\t                     (fn [e]\n377\t                       (do (cell/set! hit true)\n378\t                           (if (py/truthy\n379\t                                 (py/call exit\n380\t                                          (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] (py/type-of e)) e)\n381\t                                                    :py/None)))\n382\t                             :py/None\n383\t                             (py/raise e))))\n384\t                     (fn [] :py/None)))\n385\t           (fn [x]\n386\t             (if (cell/get hit)\n387\t               :py/None\n388\t               (py/call exit (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] :py/None) :py/None)\n389\t                                       :py/None)))))))]\n390\t\n391\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- generators\n392\t    ;; A generator is a cell holding {:py/type :generator :name s :state st}\n393\t    ;; and the slots of its state, nothing else (every transition rebuilds\n394\t    ;; the content, so no slot outlives its state):\n395\t    ;;   :created    :body      (fn [g] ...), the function body\n396\t    ;;   :suspended  :resume    the continuation captured at the yield\n397\t    ;;               :ctx       the generator's own dynamic context\n398\t    ;;   :running    :return    the active switch's continuation\n399\t    ;;               :caller-ctx the switching caller's dynamic context\n400\t    ;;   :closed     nothing\n401\t    ;; The generator owns its dynamic context (handler stack and its\n402\t    ;; depth relative to :base), so every snapshot the C1 forms take inside\n403\t    ;; the body is of that record and resumes from any caller depth. Every\n404\t    ;; crossing in sets :base to the resumer's absolute depth plus one, the\n405\t    ;; generator's own frame, so depth measures the current continuation;\n406\t    ;; every way back restores the caller's record whole, so no depth leaks\n407\t    ;; across the crossing in either directi