{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_HRMJ34Qc4SQzJ5kfkx8aXGFp","content":"src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2214:(def kind-module\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2215-  \"The `kind` host module's exports, symbol to host function: the irreducible\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2216-   kind and name primitives (see the library notes). Every export is pure.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2217-  (merge\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2218-    {'symbol? symbol?\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2219-     'keyword? keyword?\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2220-     'name name\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2221-     'symbol symbol\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2222-     'keyword keyword\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2223-     'str str\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2224-     'int? int?\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2225-     'with-meta with-meta\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2226-     'meta meta}\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2227-    #?(:clj {'var? var?} :default {})))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2228-\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2229-\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2230:(def kind-arities\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2231-  \"The published arities of each `kind` export.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2232-  {'symbol? [1], 'keyword? [1], 'name [1], 'symbol [1 2], 'keyword [1 2]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2233-   'str [0 1 2 3 4 5 6 :variadic], 'int? [1], 'var? [1], 'with-meta [2], 'meta [1]})\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2234-\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2235-\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2236-(def library\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2237-  \"The library's definitions, in order, as quoted source.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2238-  '[(defn identity\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2239-      [x]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2240-      x)\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2241-    (defn inc\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2242-      [x]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2243-      (+ x 1))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2244-    (defn dec\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2245-      [x]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2246-      (- x 1))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2247-    (defn second\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2248-      [x]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2249-      (first (rest x)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2250-    (defn not=\n--\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2551:(defn library-for\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2552-  \"The definitions of `library` that `forms` need: those whose names `forms`\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2553-   mention (outside quoted data), and the ones those mention in turn, in\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2554-   library order. Compiling only these keeps a program small.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2555-  [forms]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2556-  (let [by-name (into {} (map (fn [f] [(second f) f])) library)\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2557-        mentions (fn mentions\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2558-                   [form]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2559-                   (cond\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2560-                     (symbol? form) #{form}\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2561-                     (seq? form) (if (= 'quote (first form))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2562-                                   #{}\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2563-                                   (into #{} (mapcat mentions) form))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2564-                     (coll? form) (into #{} (mapcat mentions) form)\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2565-                     :else #{}))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2566-        defined (into #{} (comp (filter seq?) (filter #(= 'defn (first %))) (map second)) forms)\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2567-        needed (loop [todo (remove defined (mentions forms)), seen #{}]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2568-                 (if (empty? todo)\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2569-                   seen\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2570-                   (let [n (first todo)]\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc-2571-                     (if (or (contains? seen n) (not (contains? by-name n)))"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"The Python runtime already routes foreign callables through `yang.call`. I’m adding its module-dictionary projection first; the Clojure profile will use its existing argument-vector/outcome convention rather than introducing a new calling path.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_lSeh3KdK6TtMRXJ6ociPJ7Sj","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\[py/run-main|\\\\[py/run-module\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-A\":20,\"head_limit\":80}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_GlQAZ2fc2LKNtbsxjPAL6r9G","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc\",\"n_lines\":150}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_7iSYV7HjNeWwiFY80dWkqyEn","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\",\"n_lines\":130}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_8mk4ryn7XIEBomBfEI2DejIt","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc\",\"n_lines\":220}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_XZT0ucKCMiNnRhTXAKhJDVdt","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/README.md\",\"n_lines\":180}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_XZT0ucKCMiNnRhTXAKhJDVdt","content":"1\t## ClojureDart Test Suite\n2\t\n3\tClojureDart tests are cross-compiled to Dart and executed using the Dart VM.\n4\t\n5\t### Running ClojureDart Tests\n6\t```bash\n7\tclj -M:clojuredart:cljd test            # all namespaces (sweeps the classpath)\n8\tclj -M:clojuredart:cljd test some.ns    # a subset\n9\t```\n10\tThe native `cljd.build` test command compiles every `.cljc`/`.cljd` namespace on the classpath, generates a `*_test.dart` entrypoint under `test/cljd-out/` for each namespace containing deftests, and runs them via `flutter test`. There is no allowlist: JVM-only namespaces are excluded at the reader level with `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` guards (a plain `#?(:clj ...)` does NOT exclude code from the ClojureDart build, because the host pass also matches `:clj`).\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## ClojureScript Test Suite\n15\t\n16\tClojureScript tests are cross-compiled to JavaScript and executed using Node.js.\n17\t\n18\t### Running ClojureScript Tests\n19\t```bash\n20\t./bin/run-cljs-tests.sh\n21\t```\n22\tThis script uses `shadow-cljs` to compile the `:test` build and runs the resulting script with `node`.\n23\t\n24\t### Supported Test Build\n25\tThe configuration for the test build is defined in `shadow-cljs.edn` under the `:test` key.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## Yin VM Formal Test Suite\n30\t\n31\t## Overview\n32\t\n33\tFormal test suite using `clojure.test` for the Yin Virtual Machine implementation.\n34\t\n35\t## Test Files\n36\t\n37\t### [yin/vm_basic_test.clj](yin/vm_basic_test.clj)\n38\tCore functionality tests covering:\n39\t- ✅ **Literal evaluation** - Numbers and strings\n40\t- ✅ **Variable lookup** - Environment binding\n41\t- ✅ **Lambda/Closure creation** - Captures environment\n42\t- ✅ **Primitive addition** - Direct function application\n43\t- ✅ **Lambda addition** - User-defined functions\n44\t- ✅ **Increment with continuations** - Step-by-step execution\n45\t- ✅ **All arithmetic primitives** - `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`\n46\t- ✅ **All comparison operations** - `=`, `<`, `>`\n47\t\n48\t**Stats:** 8 tests, 16 assertions\n49\t\n50\t## Running Tests\n51\t\n52\t### Quick Run\n53\t```bash\n54\t./run_formal_tests.sh\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t### Manual Run\n58\t```bash\n59\tclj -M:test -e \"(require 'yin.vm-basic-test) (clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.vm-basic-test)\"\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\t### From REPL\n63\t```clojure\n64\t(require 'yin.vm-basic-test)\n65\t(clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.vm-basic-test)\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\t### Run Specific Test\n69\t```clojure\n70\t(require 'yin.vm-basic-test)\n71\t(clojure.test/test-var #'yin.vm-basic-test/test-lambda-addition)\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t## Test Structure\n75\t\n76\tEach test follows the standard `clojure.test` pattern:\n77\t\n78\t```clojure\n79\t(deftest test-name\n80\t  (testing \"Description\"\n81\t    (let [ast {...}\n82\t          result (walker/run (walker/make-state env) ast)]\n83\t      (is (= expected (:value result))\n84\t          \"Assertion message\"))))\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\t## Test Coverage\n88\t\n89\t### Covered Features\n90\t- ✅ CESK machine state transitions\n91\t- ✅ Literal value evaluation\n92\t- ✅ Variable environment lookup\n93\t- ✅ Closure creation and application\n94\t- ✅ Primitive function application\n95\t- ✅ Lambda function application\n96\t- ✅ Continuation-based evaluation\n97\t- ✅ All arithmetic operations\n98\t- ✅ All comparison operations\n99\t\n100\t### Known Limitations\n101\t- ⚠️ Nested lambda applications (requires continuation improvements)\n102\t- ⚠️ Nested arithmetic expressions within lambda bodies\n103\t- ⚠️ Conditional (if/then/else) - not yet tested\n104\t\n105\t## Configuration\n106\t\n107\tTests use the `:test` alias from `deps.edn`:\n108\t\n109\t```clojure\n110\t:test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n111\t       :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n112\t                    {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}}\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t## Test Output\n116\t\n117\tSuccessful run shows:\n118\t```\n119\tTesting yin.vm-basic-test\n120\t\n121\tRan 8 tests containing 16 assertions.\n122\t0 failures, 0 errors.\n123\t```\n124\t\n125\t## Integration with CI/CD\n126\t\n127\tThese tests can be integrated into CI/CD pipelines:\n128\t\n129\t```bash\n130\t# Exit with error code on test failure\n131\tclj -M:test -e \"(require 'yin.vm-basic-test) (let [result (clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.vm-basic-test)] (System/exit (if (clojure.test/successful? result) 0 1)))\"\n132\t```\n133\t\n134\t## Adding New Tests\n135\t\n136\t1. Create test file in `test/yin/`\n137\t2. Use namespace: `(ns yin.your-test (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]] [yin.vm :as vm]))`\n138\t3. Add tests using `deftest`, `testing`, and `is`\n139\t4. Run with: `clj -M:test -e \"(require 'yin.your-test) (clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.your-test)\"`\n140\t\n141\t## Related Documentation\n142\t\n143\t- **Implementation:** [src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc](../src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc)\n144\t- **Informal Tests:** [test_add.clj](../test_add.clj), [test_simple_continuation.clj](../test_simple_continuation.clj)\n145\t- **Full Documentation:** [YIN_VM_TESTS.md](../YIN_VM_TESTS.md)"}
