{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_8mk4ryn7XIEBomBfEI2DejIt","content":"1\t(ns yang.core.module\n2\t  \"Module emitter machinery shared by every language frontend\n3\t   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L3): the linker module naming\n4\t   rule, the `require` and wide-application tree nodes, free-name\n5\t   declaration over a host registry, and the `module-spec` and SCC bundle\n6\t   shapes `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` takes. A language supplies\n7\t   its prefix, its runtime module and its module AST; nothing here knows a\n8\t   source language.\"\n9\t  (:require\n10\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n11\t    [yang.core.prelude :as prelude]\n12\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n13\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\n14\t    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n15\t\n16\t\n17\t(defn module-symbol\n18\t  \"The linker module name of source module `name` under language `prefix`\n19\t   (\\\"py\\\", \\\"php\\\", \\\"js\\\"): `<prefix>m.` then the name with each dot a `$`,\n20\t   so no linker module name is a dotted prefix of another.\"\n21\t  [prefix name]\n22\t  (symbol (str prefix \"m.\" (str/replace name \".\" \"$\"))))\n23\t\n24\t\n25\t(defn require-node\n26\t  \"(require 'm) as a tree node.\"\n27\t  [m]\n28\t  (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote m))))\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t(defn module-tree\n32\t  \"A wide application: all definitions remain at module level.\"\n33\t  [operands]\n34\t  (prelude/wide-app operands))\n35\t\n36\t\n37\t(defn declare-free-name\n38\t  \"The `:primitives` entry free name `n` declares over `registry`, or nil\n39\t   when `covered` (the requirement-pinned module names) covers it. A name\n40\t   no `vm/primitives` profile or host export supplies throws, with\n41\t   `refusal` under `refusal-key` in its data.\"\n42\t  [refusal-key refusal registry covered n]\n43\t  (if (and (symbol? n) (some? (namespace n))\n44\t           (contains? covered (symbol (namespace n))))\n45\t    nil\n46\t    (if-let [profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives n)]\n47\t      [n profile]\n48\t      (if-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n49\t        (let [entry (module/module-entry (:modules registry)\n50\t                                         (symbol (namespace n)))\n51\t              f (get-in entry [:slice (symbol (name n))])]\n52\t          [n {:yin.k/profile address,\n53\t              :yin.k/effects\n54\t              (get (:callable-effects registry) f #{})}])\n55\t        (throw (ex-info \"the module reads an undeclared name\"\n56\t                        {refusal-key refusal, :name n}))))))\n57\t\n58\t\n59\t(defn free-primitives\n60\t  \"The `:primitives` map declaring every free name of `ast` over `registry`.\"\n61\t  [refusal-key refusal registry covered ast]\n62\t  (let [free (remove (conj (prelude/defined-keys ast) 'yin/def)\n63\t                     (prelude/free-names ast))]\n64\t    (into {}\n65\t          (keep (partial declare-free-name refusal-key refusal registry covered))\n66\t          (sort-by str free))))\n67\t\n68\t\n69\t(defn module-spec\n70\t  \"`publish-module!`'s spec for module `name`: `ast` with `exports`, requiring\n71\t   the runtime module `runtime-name` at `runtime-address` and each of `deps`\n72\t   ({module-symbol address}). A free name under a required module is covered\n73\t   by it; any other is declared as `declare-free-name` does.\"\n74\t  [refusal-key refusal registry\n75\t   {:keys [name ast exports runtime-name runtime-address deps]}]\n76\t  (let [requires (into {runtime-name runtime-address} deps)]\n77\t    {:name name,\n78\t     :ast ast,\n79\t     :exports exports,\n80\t     :requires requires,\n81\t     :primitives (free-primitives refusal-key refusal registry\n82\t                                  (set (keys requires)) ast)}))\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn alias-spec\n86\t  \"A thin member alias of the SCC bundle `bundle-name`: it requires the\n87\t   bundle and defines `spec` and `body` as the bundle's `spec-key` and\n88\t   `body-key` exports.\"\n89\t  [name exports require-profile bundle-name spec-key body-key]\n90\t  {:name name,\n91\t   :exports exports,\n92\t   :primitives {'require require-profile},\n93\t   :ast (module-tree\n94\t          [(require-node bundle-name)\n95\t           (u/def! 'spec (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str spec-key))))\n96\t           (u/def! 'body (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str body-key))))])})\n97\t\n98\t\n99\t(defn scc-module-specs\n100\t  \"The SCC publication shape: the `bundle` spec first, then the member alias\n101\t   specs (each `alias-spec`'s output) in member order.\"\n102\t  [bundle aliases]\n103\t  (into [bundle] aliases))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_GlQAZ2fc2LKNtbsxjPAL6r9G","content":"1\t(ns yang.python.antlr.render\n2\t  \"Python text for the values a program printed, derived at the boundary\n3\t   from the plain-data snapshots `py/print` collects (the same place owner\n4\t   decision 2 puts traceback line numbers). Portable and deterministic: a\n5\t   float arrives tagged `{:py/float x}`, so `4/2` prints `2.0` on every\n6\t   host, JS included.\n7\t\n8\t   Float repr is CPython's on every host and for every double: the\n9\t   shortest round-trip digits come from the `integer` module's\n10\t   `float-digits` (version 4), never from host `str`, in fixed notation\n11\t   when the decimal exponent is from -4 to 15 and in exponent notation\n12\t   otherwise.\"\n13\t  (:require\n14\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n15\t    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n16\t    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n17\t\n18\t\n19\t(def ^:private exact\n20\t  \"The `integer` exports with limits no snapshot reaches: the renderer\n21\t   writes an integer's exact decimal with no digit limit, as CPython\n22\t   3.9.6 prints it (a limit on `print` belongs to guest `str`), and a\n23\t   float's shortest digits.\"\n24\t  (integer/integer-module {::integer/max-bits 9007199254740991,\n25\t                           ::integer/max-digits 9007199254740991}))\n26\t\n27\t\n28\t(defn- negative-zero?\n29\t  [x]\n30\t  (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1.0 x))))\n31\t\n32\t\n33\t(defn- zeros\n34\t  [n]\n35\t  (apply str (repeat n \"0\")))\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t(defn- exponent-text\n39\t  \"CPython's exponent: `e`, a sign, and at least two digits.\"\n40\t  [e]\n41\t  (let [digits (str (if (neg? e) (- e) e))]\n42\t    (str (if (neg? e) \"e-\" \"e+\")\n43\t         (if (< (count digits) 2) (str \"0\" digits) digits))))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(defn- digits-repr\n47\t  \"CPython's `repr` of |v| = d1.d2...dn x 10^`e`: fixed notation when\n48\t   -4 <= e < 16, with `.0` when there is no fraction, else `d[.ddd]`\n49\t   and the exponent.\"\n50\t  [digits e]\n51\t  (let [n (count digits)]\n52\t    (cond\n53\t      (and (<= 0 e) (< e 16))\n54\t      (if (<= n (inc e))\n55\t        (str digits (zeros (- (inc e) n)) \".0\")\n56\t        (str (subs digits 0 (inc e)) \".\" (subs digits (inc e))))\n57\t      (and (<= -4 e) (< e 0))\n58\t      (str \"0.\" (zeros (dec (- e))) digits)\n59\t      :else\n60\t      (str (subs digits 0 1)\n61\t           (when (> n 1) (str \".\" (subs digits 1)))\n62\t           (exponent-text e)))))\n63\t\n64\t\n65\t(defn float-repr\n66\t  \"Python repr of float `f`, a host number or float64 content (on JS,\n67\t   Jing's carrier).\"\n68\t  [f]\n69\t  (let [x (data/float-value f)]\n70\t    (cond\n71\t      #?(:cljd (.-isNaN ^num x)\n72\t         :clj (Double/isNaN x)\n73\t         :cljs (js/isNaN x))\n74\t      \"nan\"\n75\t      (= x ##Inf) \"inf\"\n76\t      (= x ##-Inf) \"-inf\"\n77\t      (zero? x) (if (negative-zero? x) \"-0.0\" \"0.0\")\n78\t      :else (let [[digits e] ((get exact 'float-digits) x)]\n79\t              (str (when (neg? x) \"-\") (digits-repr digits e))))))\n80\t\n81\t\n82\t(declare repr)\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn- code-unit\n86\t  [s i]\n87\t  #?(:cljd (.codeUnitAt ^String s i)\n88\t     :clj (int (.charAt ^String s (int i)))\n89\t     :cljs (.charCodeAt s i)))\n90\t\n91\t\n92\t(defn- hex2\n93\t  [n]\n94\t  (let [digits \"0123456789abcdef\"]\n95\t    (str (subs digits (quot n 16) (inc (quot n 16)))\n96\t         (subs digits (rem n 16) (inc (rem n 16))))))\n97\t\n98\t\n99\t(defn string-repr\n100\t  \"Python's str repr: single quotes unless the text has a single quote and\n101\t   no double quote; backslash, the quote, \\\\n \\\\r \\\\t and other control\n102\t   characters escaped.\"\n103\t  [s]\n104\t  (let [q (if (and (str/includes? s \"'\") (not (str/includes? s \"\\\"\"))) \"\\\"\" \"'\")]\n105\t    (str q\n106\t         (apply str\n107\t                (map (fn [i]\n108\t                       (let [c (code-unit s i)\n109\t                             ch (subs s i (inc i))]\n110\t                         (cond\n111\t                           (= ch \"\\\\\") \"\\\\\\\\\"\n112\t                           (= ch q) (str \"\\\\\" q)\n113\t                           (= c 10) \"\\\\n\"\n114\t                           (= c 13) \"\\\\r\"\n115\t                           (= c 9) \"\\\\t\"\n116\t                           (or (< c 32) (= c 127)) (str \"\\\\x\" (hex2 c))\n117\t                           :else ch)))\n118\t                     (range (count s))))\n119\t         q)))\n120\t\n121\t\n122\t(defn- seq-repr\n123\t  [open close xs]\n124\t  (str open (str/join \", \" (map repr xs)) close))\n125\t\n126\t\n127\t(defn repr\n128\t  \"Python `repr` of one snapshot value.\"\n129\t  [v]\n130\t  (cond\n131\t    (nil? v) \"None\"\n132\t    (true? v) \"True\"\n133\t    (false? v) \"False\"\n134\t    (string? v) (string-repr v)\n135\t    ;; every exact carrier, a JS or Dart BigInt included, which `number?`\n136\t    ;; misses\n137\t    ((get exact 'integer?) v) ((get exact 'format) v)\n138\t    (number? v) (str v)\n139\t    (vector? v) (seq-repr \"[\" \"]\" v)\n140\t    (map? v)\n141\t    (cond\n142\t      (contains? v :py/float) (float-repr (:py/float v))\n143\t      (contains? v :py/tuple) (let [xs (:py/tuple v)]\n144\t                                (if (= 1 (count xs))\n145\t                                  (str \"(\" (repr (first xs)) \",)\")\n146\t                                  (seq-repr \"(\" \")\" xs)))\n147\t      (contains? v :py/dict) (str \"{\"\n148\t                                  (str/join \", \"\n149\t                                            (map (fn [[k x]]\n150\t                                                   (str (repr k) \": \" (repr x)))"}
