{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_9Xr6ff1qUyrCFHZtiPzQT60G","content":"1\t(ns yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness\n2\t  \"The linked profile's composition for the JavaScript tests (T1 step S5,\n3\t   docs/design/yang.typescript.md section 13): the namespace that requires\n4\t   this is the publisher of `js` and `jssp`, so it publishes each module\n5\t   once per process into one in-memory content store and serves them to\n6\t   every linked run over a `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under\n7\t   `:trusted` derivation (the remediation ruling's R6). The `:verifying`\n8\t   evidence is `publish-module!`'s own `link-local` links, which\n9\t   `linked-prelude-test` asserts.\n10\t\n11\t   A linked run builds the program's task on one of the three vector VMs\n12\t   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately\n13\t   until the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker\n14\t   is not a backend here: its link of `js` is refused `:undeclared-free`\n15\t   until L-b.\"\n16\t  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n17\t            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n18\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n19\t            [yang.core.call :as call]\n20\t            [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n21\t            [yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n22\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n23\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n24\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n25\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n26\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n27\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n28\t            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n29\t            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n30\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n31\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n32\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n33\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n34\t\n35\t\n36\t(def integer-limits\n37\t  \"The ordinary JavaScript composition's `integer` limits.\"\n38\t  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n39\t\n40\t\n41\t(defn registry\n42\t  \"The full host registry a linked JavaScript composition registers: the\n43\t   `require` handler, then `cell`, `data`, `integer` under `limits`, and\n44\t   `stream` — the hook module `jssp` polls a signal stream, so the\n45\t   safepointed composition needs it even though `js` does not.\"\n46\t  ([] (registry integer-limits))\n47\t  ([limits]\n48\t   (-> (module/default-registry)\n49\t       module/register-cell-module\n50\t       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n51\t       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n52\t       module/register-stream-module)))\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t(def published\n56\t  \"`js` published once into its own content store:\n57\t   `{:store s :result r :address a :call-address ca}`. `yang.call` is\n58\t   published first so `js` pins its shared calling runtime.\"\n59\t  (delay\n60\t    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n61\t          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n62\t          result (publish/publish-module! store\n63\t                                          (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n64\t                                                               (:address call-result)))]\n65\t      {:store store,\n66\t       :result result,\n67\t       :address (:address result),\n68\t       :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n69\t\n70\t\n71\t(def published-jssp\n72\t  \"`jssp` published once into `js`'s own content store, which its pinned\n73\t   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n74\t  (delay\n75\t    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n76\t          result (publish/publish-module!\n77\t                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n78\t      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n79\t\n80\t\n81\t(defn source\n82\t  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` defaults\n83\t   to `{js <address> yang.call <address>}`, derivation `:trusted`, the test\n84\t   being the publisher. `jssp`-serving sources pass their own `name-env`.\"\n85\t  ([] (source {'js (:address @published),\n86\t               'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n87\t  ([name-env]\n88\t   (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n89\t                      :name-env name-env,\n90\t                      :derivation :trusted})))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(defn safepoint-source\n94\t  \"The serving composition over the published modules: `jssp` requires\n95\t   `js`, and `js` requires `yang.call`.\"\n96\t  []\n97\t  (source {'js (:address @published),\n98\t           'jssp (:address @published-jssp),\n99\t           'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n100\t"}
