{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_NJlnt7uRS1T4ofhRno0ZZF42","content":"35\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\n36\t    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\n37\t    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\n38\t    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\n39\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n40\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n41\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n42\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n43\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(def ^:private published-php\n47\t  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n48\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n49\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n50\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n51\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n52\t\n53\t\n54\t(defn- parse-ok\n55\t  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n56\t  [parse source]\n57\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\n58\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n59\t      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n60\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n61\t    pk))\n62\t\n63\t\n64\t(def frontends\n65\t  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n66\t\n67\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n68\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n69\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n70\t   - `:unit`: packet to the unmodified lowered unit, the function its\n71\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\n72\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n73\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table);\n74\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n75\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name (a JS global, a PHP\n76\t     function);\n77\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n78\t  {:typescript\n79\t   {:runtime 'js,\n80\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\n81\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\n82\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\n83\t    :unit #(names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit %)),\n84\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\n85\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\n86\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\n87\t    :render render/output},\n88\t   :php\n89\t   {:runtime 'php,\n90\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\n91\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\n92\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\n93\t    :unit #(u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body %)),\n94\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\n95\t    :read-export (fn [export]\n96\t                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\n97\t    :project (fn [name value]\n98\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n99\t    :render php-h/render}})\n100\t\n101\t\n102\t(defn- profile\n103\t  [frontend]\n104\t  (or (get frontends frontend)"}
